{"parentUuid":"a8397718-9c82-43b3-a154-68ae8ac80cee","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_016epGhCc18DbW4bHVBTStBz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Plot twist — the SQL isn't the bottleneck. Here's what direct-to-DB measurements reveal:\n\n| Operation (7d, direct via mysql2) | Time | Rows |\n|---|---|---|\n| me-side query (original SQL) | **433ms** | 155 (75 distinct cps) |\n| team-side query (original SQL) | **546ms** | **1000 (hit LIMIT)** |\n| analyses fetch (selectAll, all JSON) | **204ms** | 3 |\n| **Total raw DB work** | **~1.2s** | — |\n\nBut the `/me/recap` HTTP call took **~44s** for the same window. That's a **35× slowdown that has nothing to do with the SQL** — the queries finish in ~1s direct.\n\n`★ Insight ─────────────────────────────────────`\n- **The real culprit is almost certainly wrangler dev's local hyperdrive emulator** (or its workerd/V8 boundary). When wrangler runs locally, every DB query crosses: workerd → hyperdrive emulator (Node) → mysql2 → AWS PlanetScale → back. Each hop has serialization cost, and the local emulator isn't optimized like production Cloudflare workers are. In production, Workers run *next to* PlanetScale via real hyperdrive with sub-ms RTT and proper pooling.\n- **The team-side query is hitting the 1000-row LIMIT** — meaning there's >1000 team checkpoints in 7d on your active repos. That 1000-row list goes through `aggregateCheckpointsByAgent` and `mergeAnalysesInto` in JS, which the workerd runtime then has to JSON-serialize on the way out. Volume × wrangler-dev overhead = 44s.\n- **Restructuring the SQL would shave ~100ms** at best. Worth it eventually, but it won't move the 44s number measured through wrangler dev.\n`─────────────────────────────────────────────────`\n\n## What this changes\n\nI was about to write a query refactor that EXPLAIN said would be cleaner, but the data says it would barely register. Before changing any code, the right move is:\n\n**Hit the actually-deployed staging API and measure there.** If staging-deployed serves `/me/recap?7d` in ~1-2s, the production behavior is fine and we don't need to change anything for #1604 to ship. The 44s is a wrangler-dev artifact.\n\nIf staging-deployed *also* takes 30s+, then the fix isn't SQL — it's probably:\n1. The team-side query needs a tighter limit (1000 is a lot for an aggregate)\n2. `mergeAnalysesInto` could `Promise.all` me + team (~200ms saved either way)\n3. We may need to push label/skill counting into SQL via `GROUP BY` instead of pulling full analysis_json to JS\n\n## Proposal\n\nWant me to hit deployed staging directly to compare? I'd point a curl at whatever the staging URL is (or `entire.io` itself if there's no separate staging). That tells us in 30 seconds whether to change code or just merge."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":674,"cache_read_input_tokens":263168,"output_tokens":2589,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":674,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":2589,"cache_read_input_tokens":263168,"cache_creation_input_tokens":674,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":674},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CaUJPgBQbe7FCzVmFoRsK","type":"assistant","uuid":"68fd0b03-25d9-4fa2-8fcb-b1d670caf7b7","timestamp":"2026-04-27T12:47:56.680Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/entire-activity","sessionId":"a654b6ca-4957-4d7c-8c99-62db313ff0a0","version":"2.1.119","gitBranch":"entire-activity"}
