{"parentUuid":"b797bbf4-07fd-4f00-8047-9160e898b729","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_017mrYuMotu33SgyKYTGL7GC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Got the smoking gun:**\n\n```\ngetUser:                     3ms\ngetByUser (me-side):       1.5s   ← reasonable\ngetTeamOnUserRepos:         50s   ← 99% OF THE TOTAL TIME\nmergeAnalyses (both):      0.3s   ← cheap (Promise.all helps)\nTOTAL:                      50s\n```\n\nThe me-side query takes 1.5s through wrangler, but the **team-side query alone takes 50 seconds** — for the same code that took 0.5s direct via mysql2. So wrangler-dev's hyperdrive emulator is paying a 100× penalty *specifically* on the team-side query.\n\n`★ Insight ─────────────────────────────────────`\n- **The penalty correlates with row volume, not query complexity**. Me-side returns 155 rows → 1.5s wrangler vs 0.4s raw (≈4× overhead, same as /me/activity). Team-side returns 1000 rows → 50s wrangler vs 0.5s raw (≈100× overhead). So wrangler dev's hyperdrive emulator scales *non-linearly* with result-set size — almost certainly due to per-row marshalling across the workerd ↔ Node boundary.\n- **Production won't have this problem at all.** Real Cloudflare Workers + hyperdrive don't cross that workerd/Node bridge — the worker IS workerd, hyperdrive is in-process. The 50s here is purely an emulator artifact. The /me/activity production timings (1s for similar work) are the real reference point.\n- **But there's still real work to do** — the team-side query returning 1000 raw rows is wasteful regardless of environment. We're fetching all that just to GROUP BY agent and count labels/skills. Pushing the aggregation into SQL would be ~1KB of result instead of ~500KB, helps prod throughput too.\n`─────────────────────────────────────────────────`\n\n## Three options\n\n1. **Ship as-is.** The 50s is wrangler-dev only. Production will be ~1-2s for `/me/recap` based on `/me/activity` precedent. PR #1604 isn't blocked. We move on.\n2. **Cap team-side limit to 200** (one-line change). Cuts wrangler-dev time ~5× to ~10s. Risk: silently undercounts agents when team has >200 checkpoints in a window. Bad for accuracy.\n3. **Push aggregation into SQL** (real refactor — replace `getTeamOnUserRepos` returning rows with an aggregating version that returns per-agent totals + a thin list of checkpoint_ids for the analyses fetch). Maybe a 1-hour change. Helps both wrangler dev *and* production payload size. Right thing to do, but bigger.\n\nMy read: **option 1 is the correct ship decision, option 3 is the right follow-up.** The wrangler-dev numbers we've been chasing are misleading for the production question — we now have evidence that the actual bottleneck disappears in production.\n\nWant to call it done on the perf side and move forward, or do you want me to actually do option 3?"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":976,"cache_read_input_tokens":294635,"output_tokens":5014,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":976,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":5014,"cache_read_input_tokens":294635,"cache_creation_input_tokens":976,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":976},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CaUM6LyPEhzccisuyWNne","type":"assistant","uuid":"8ed5c021-b975-49d7-9890-7a4808782d53","timestamp":"2026-04-27T13:23:52.040Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/entire-activity","sessionId":"a654b6ca-4957-4d7c-8c99-62db313ff0a0","version":"2.1.119","gitBranch":"entire-activity"}
