{"parentUuid":"8169a2fa-12d2-47e3-a64c-3bfbf1469df9","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"c6696658-c389-408e-ba29-ea5243870014","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Pq6z7dWGc9KUg844XFC7nf","type":"tool_result","content":"=== PR #1604 metadata ===\n{\n    \"number\": 1604,\n    \"reviewDecision\": \"REVIEW_REQUIRED\",\n    \"state\": \"OPEN\",\n    \"title\": \"feat(api): /api/v1/me/recap endpoint for per-agent recap aggregates\",\n    \"url\": \"https://github.com/entirehq/entire.io/pull/1604\"\n}\n\n=== PR-level review comments ===\n{\"body\":\"## Pull request overview\\n\\nAdds a new authenticated `GET /api/v1/me/recap` endpoint that returns per-agent recap aggregates (and optionally “you vs team” contributor-side aggregates) and wires it through OpenAPI + generated frontend SDK.\\n\\n**Changes:**\\n- Introduces `api/src/routes/recap.ts` and mounts\",\"state\":\"COMMENTED\",\"submitted_at\":\"2026-04-27T07:20:28Z\",\"user\":\"copilot-pull-request-reviewer[bot]\"}\n\n=== inline review comments (line-level) ===\n{\"body\":\"The handler always runs `getTeamOnUserRepos(...)` even when `repo` is not provided. Per PR description/types, the contributors side should be disabled when `repo` is absent; skipping this query would also avoid unnecessary DB work on the common cross-repo case.\",\"line\":180,\"path\":\"api/src/routes/recap.ts\",\"user\":\"Copilot\"}\n{\"body\":\"`contributors` is typed/documented as nullable (and the PR description says it should be `null` when `?repo=` is omitted), but the response always returns a non-null summary object. Consider returning `contributors: null` (and per-agent `contributors: null`) when `repoParam` is not provided.\",\"line\":237,\"path\":\"api/src/routes/recap.ts\",\"user\":\"Copilot\"}\n{\"body\":\"`distinctUsers` is computed from distinct `commit_sha` values, which counts commits rather than contributors. This will significantly overcount (or otherwise misreport) contributor count. To make this correct, include an author identifier in the team checkpoint rows (e.g., `commit_author_github_id`) or compute the distinct contributor count via a dedicated DB query.\",\"line\":216,\"path\":\"api/src/routes/recap.ts\",\"user\":\"Copilot\"}\n{\"body\":\"`analysesById` is keyed only by `checkpoint_id`, but `checkpoint_id` is only unique per repo (DB has a unique constraint on (repo_id, checkpoint_id)). If two repos share the same checkpoint_id, this map can overwrite analyses and attach the wrong analysis to a checkpoint when merging. Key the map by `(repo_id, checkpoint_id)` (e.g., `${repo_id}:${checkpoint_id}`) and look it up using both values.\",\"line\":351,\"path\":\"api/src/routes/recap.ts\",\"user\":\"Copilot\"}\n{\"body\":\"`parseRecapWindow` supports `since`/`until` query params, but the route’s OpenAPI `parameters` (and the generated frontend SDK types) only document `timeframe`/`repo`/`limit`. If the CLI/frontends are meant to use `since`/`until`, add them to `describeRoute` (and OpenAPI) with validation; otherwise consider removing this undocumented behavior to avoid a hidden API surface.\\n```suggestion\\n// parseRe\",\"line\":263,\"path\":\"api/src/routes/recap.ts\",\"user\":\"Copilot\"}\n{\"body\":\"There are unit tests for other `me` endpoints (see `api/src/routes/me.test.ts`), but this new recap endpoint currently has no route-level unit tests. Adding a small `recap.test.ts` covering repo scoping, the `contributors` null/non-null behavior, and analysis merging would help prevent regressions in these aggregation semantics.\",\"line\":106,\"path\":\"api/src/routes/recap.ts\",\"user\":\"Copilot\"}\n{\"body\":\"The header comment says tokens are “intentionally omitted”, but the response schema and implementation include `tokens` (and top-level `contributors.totalTokens` is derived from them). Please update the comment to match the actual payload to avoid confusion for future maintainers.\\n```suggestion\\n//   - me side: checkpoints + tokens + transcriptTokens + filesChanged\\n//     + labels + skills + mcpSer\",\"line\":6,\"path\":\"api/src/routes/recap.ts\",\"user\":\"Copilot\"}\n{\"body\":\"When `repo` is provided, the code fetches up to `limit` checkpoints across *all* repos and only then filters by `repo_full_name`. This can return an incomplete recap for the requested repo (the relevant checkpoints may be pushed out by other repos before the LIMIT), and it also makes the contributors side incomplete for the same reason. Apply the repo constraint in the DB query (or add repo-scoped\",\"line\":186,\"path\":\"api/src/routes/recap.ts\",\"user\":\"Copilot\"}\n\n=== general issue comments on PR ===\n{\"body\":\"## Deploying with \\u0026nbsp;\\u003ca href=\\\"https://workers.dev\\\"\\u003e\\u003cimg alt=\\\"Cloudflare Workers\\\" src=\\\"https://workers.cloudflare.com/logo.svg\\\" width=\\\"16\\\"\\u003e\\u003c/a\\u003e \\u0026nbsp;Cloudflare Workers\\nThe latest updates on your project. Learn more about [integrating Git with Workers](https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/ci-\",\"user\":\"cloudflare-workers-and-pages[bot]\"}\nShell cwd was reset to /Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/entire-activity","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"e000d0a5-a112-446c-892f-b02f86d5bc94","timestamp":"2026-04-27T15:37:52.267Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"=== PR #1604 metadata ===\n{\n    \"number\": 1604,\n    \"reviewDecision\": \"REVIEW_REQUIRED\",\n    \"state\": \"OPEN\",\n    \"title\": \"feat(api): /api/v1/me/recap endpoint for per-agent recap aggregates\",\n    \"url\": \"https://github.com/entirehq/entire.io/pull/1604\"\n}\n\n=== PR-level review comments ===\n{\"body\":\"## Pull request overview\\n\\nAdds a new authenticated `GET /api/v1/me/recap` endpoint that returns per-agent recap aggregates (and optionally “you vs team” contributor-side aggregates) and wires it through OpenAPI + generated frontend SDK.\\n\\n**Changes:**\\n- Introduces `api/src/routes/recap.ts` and mounts\",\"state\":\"COMM