{"parentUuid":"343675ed-60e5-4204-a6a2-97229afd9e07","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01DsgpSF576HZ9XhAk5Tw66u","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_014VeysVTNev2MUgFVfNuMuq","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/entire.io/.worktrees/recap-endpoint && \\\n  gh pr edit 1604 --body \"$(cat <<'EOF'\n<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entirehq/entire.io/trails/6038b77becfc\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\n\n## Summary\n\n- New `GET /api/v1/me/recap` endpoint returning per-agent rollups (checkpoints, tokens, transcript tokens, files changed, labels, skills, MCP servers, tool mix) for the authenticated user, plus an optional `contributors` counterpart aggregated across every contributor on a scoped repo.\n- Replaces three separate CLI calls (`GET /me/checkpoints` + `POST /checkpoints/analyses/batch` + `GET /:org/:repo/overview/*`) with one aggregate.\n- Powers the \"you vs. team\" columns in `entire recap` (CLI side: entireio/cli#1015).\n\n## Behavior\n\n- **`?repo=org/name`** — when supplied, both the me-side and team-side queries scope to that repo at the SQL level. The response's `contributors` field (top-level + per-agent) carries the team aggregate.\n- **No `?repo=`** — me-side aggregates span every repo the user has checkpoints on; team-side is **skipped** entirely (no coherent \"everyone else\" reference frame across repos), and `contributors` is `null` both top-level and per-agent.\n- **`?since=…&until=…`** — ISO-8601 explicit window, takes precedence over `timeframe`. Used by the CLI so its `--day`/`--week`/`--month` ranges line up exactly with the server aggregation window.\n- **`?timeframe=last-month|last-3-months|last-6-months`** — fallback when explicit dates are absent.\n\n## Changes\n\n- `api/src/routes/recap.ts` — Hono route mounted at `/api/v1/me/recap` (bearer auth inherited from `meRoutes`). Includes per-agent aggregator + analysis-merger + daily-activity bucketing.\n- `api/src/routes/recap.test.ts` — five route-level tests: null contributors, repo scoping into both queries, distinct-author counting, since/until override, per-`(repo_id, checkpoint_id)` analysis attribution.\n- `api/src/lib/db/checkpoints.ts` + `api/src/lib/planetscale/checkpoints.ts` — `UserCheckpoint` now carries `commit_author_github_id`; `getByUser` and `getTeamOnUserRepos` accept an optional `repoFullName` so the repo filter pushes into SQL (instead of post-filtering after `LIMIT 500`).\n- `api/src/lib/db/db-types.ts` — extended signatures.\n- `api/src/lib/activity-aggregator.test.ts` — fixture updated for the new field.\n- `api/docs/openapi.json` + `frontend/src/gen/api-sdk/` — regenerated for the new params (`since`, `until`).\n\n## Review-driven fixes (since first push)\n\nResolved Copilot review on this PR + perf pass:\n\n- **perf** — me + team `mergeAnalysesInto` calls parallelized via `Promise.all`. Saves one round-trip of analysis lookups per request.\n- **correctness** — `?repo=` filter pushed into SQL (was post-filtering in JS, could lose rows past `LIMIT`).\n- **correctness** — `distinctUsers` counts distinct `commit_author_github_id`, not distinct `commit_sha` (the old count overstated by ~commits-per-author).\n- **correctness** — analyses attributed by `${repo_id}:${checkpoint_id}` (checkpoint_id is only unique inside a repo per `uq_repo_checkpoints_repo_checkpoint`).\n- **spec** — team query skipped + `contributors: null` returned when `?repo=` is absent (matches the documented contract).\n- **api surface** — `since` / `until` query params now documented in `describeRoute` + OpenAPI + SDK.\n- **doc rot** — header comment updated to match the actual payload.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] Live smoke vs. local wrangler dev (pointed at staging PlanetScale): `GET /api/v1/me/recap?repo=entireio/cli&since=…&until=…` returns populated agents with labels / skills / toolMix.\n- [x] `entire recap --vie