{"parentUuid":"2c0f5640-9005-4b8a-8d64-b8ed1e8a60dd","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01X2ZMLKEGXnCREhXK3EBCMk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Real numbers:\n\n| Setup | `/me/recap --90` |\n|---|---|\n| Local wrangler dev (current) | **>60s timeout** |\n| `/me/activity` 6mo deployed prod (similar workload) | **2.0s** |\n\nProduction `/me/recap` will likely be 2–5s based on the /me/activity ratio. For a TUI keypress, **2-5s is borderline ugly**. Local wrangler-dev is a non-issue (artifact), but production needs to be better.\n\n`★ Insight ─────────────────────────────────────`\n- The fix that eliminates perceived lag entirely without any server work is **parallel prefetch + range-keyed cache** in the TUI. At startup, fire all four ranges (`day`/`week`/`month`/`90`) in parallel. Total wait ≈ slowest single fetch (~5s in prod). After that, every range toggle is instant — toggle is just a map lookup. Users stop feeling the network at all.\n- The fix that actually makes production fast is the **option 3 SQL refactor** we discussed earlier — replace \"fetch 1000 rows then GROUP BY in JS\" with \"GROUP BY in SQL.\" Drops the team-side query from \"fetch all then count\" to \"count and return\". Likely takes prod /me/recap from 2-5s down to <500ms. Real, but a meaningful chunk of work on the server PR.\n`─────────────────────────────────────────────────`\n\n## Two-tier plan\n\n**Tier 1 — client-side (do now): parallel prefetch + cache.** Pay once at startup (~5s background), zero lag on every toggle after.\n\n```\nOn startup:\n  Promise.all over [day, week, month, 90] → store in cache map\n  Use cache.day for initial render\n  Background prefetch finishes silently\nOn range toggle:\n  Hit cache → instant render\n  Cache miss (shouldn't happen) → existing fetch path\n```\n\nConcrete: ~80 lines in tui.go + the cache map. No server change.\n\n**Tier 2 — server-side (next PR on #1604): SQL aggregation.** The team-side query stops returning 1000 rows of full checkpoint metadata. Replace with `GROUP BY agent` returning ~5-10 rows of pre-aggregated counts + a separate small query for analyses. This is the durable fix.\n\n**Recommendation:** Do Tier 1 right now in this PR — it's all in `tui.go` and ships the bug fixes immediately with great UX. Tier 2 lands as a separate server PR (you mentioned earlier you might tackle it next). Combined, range toggles feel instant in production.\n\nWant me to implement Tier 1 now?"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2115,"cache_read_input_tokens":476812,"output_tokens":1332,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2115,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":1332,"cache_read_input_tokens":476812,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2115,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2115},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CaW9e1boho4wsp1ekyMDX","type":"assistant","uuid":"fba1e586-6367-409b-b5ad-ca54ac43d045","timestamp":"2026-04-28T12:14:00.671Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/entire-activity","sessionId":"a654b6ca-4957-4d7c-8c99-62db313ff0a0","version":"2.1.119","gitBranch":"entire-activity"}
