{"parentUuid":"bf83cbed-0b5b-44da-89cb-6664d0cd208c","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01G13apMzzvnS7aDrWyDefw2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Let me present the full design in tight sections so we can lock down everything before I write the spec doc. Anything to amend, flag now.\n\n## 1. Architecture\n\nTwo PRs compose to deliver the perf+accuracy fix:\n\n| PR | Layer | What changes |\n|---|---|---|\n| `entireio/cli#1015` | **Tier 1 (client)** | Commit existing prefetch + cache-clear-on-miss code (already in worktree). Tests already pass. |\n| `entirehq/entire.io#1604` | **Tier 2 (server)** | Schema migration + analysis-queue write path + recap.ts query rewrite |\n\nNo frontend changes. No /me/activity changes. Surface area stays inside the recap endpoint.\n\n## 2. Schema\n\nThree new tables, mechanically identical, on the `entire-io` PlanetScale keyspace:\n\n```sql\nCREATE TABLE repo_checkpoint_analysis_labels (\n  repo_id       binary(16)   NOT NULL,\n  checkpoint_id varbinary(64) NOT NULL,\n  name          varchar(64)  NOT NULL,\n  count         int unsigned NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (repo_id, checkpoint_id, name),\n  KEY by_repo_name (repo_id, name)  -- supports per-repo aggregate scans\n);\n-- repo_checkpoint_analysis_skills:    same shape\n-- repo_checkpoint_analysis_tool_mix:  same shape (name = bucket: shell/fileOps/...)\n```\n\nSame indexes, same query template, same backfill logic.\n\n## 3. Write path\n\n`analysis-queue.ts` worker, when persisting a completed `repo_checkpoint_analyses` row, also batch-inserts derived facet rows into the three tables. Single transaction so the analysis JSON and its facets are always consistent. On update (re-analysis), `DELETE then INSERT` per checkpoint to avoid stale rows.\n\n## 4. Read path\n\n`recap.ts` route handler:\n- Counts (checkpoints, tokens, distinct authors): **already** SQL-aggregatable via `COUNT(*)`/`SUM`/`COUNT(DISTINCT)`. Refactor existing JS aggregator into a new `getCheckpointCountsByAgent` function returning per-agent rollups directly.\n- Qualitative (labels/skills/tool-mix): three parallel `SELECT name, SUM(count) GROUP BY name` queries against the new tables, joined to the same checkpoint-set CTE that filters by author/repo/window.\n- All four queries (counts + 3 qualitative) fire via `Promise.all`. Wallclock = max(any one) ≈ ~500ms target.\n- The existing `getByUser` / `getTeamOnUserRepos` per-row queries are deleted from the route — no longer needed once aggregation moves to SQL.\n\n## 5. Migration & backfill\n\n- Schema migration via PlanetScale schema branch + deploy request (existing repo pattern).\n- Backfill script (`scripts/backfill-analysis-facets.ts`) iterates `repo_checkpoint_analyses` where `status='complete'`, parses each `analysis_json`, batch-inserts into the three tables in chunks of 500. Idempotent (DELETE-then-INSERT per checkpoint). Runs once via `pnpm exec tsx`.\n- Worker code deployed AFTER backfill completes — no pre-deploy reads of empty tables.\n\n## 6. Error handling\n\n- Analysis JSON malformed (existing concern): backfill skips with a logged warning, write-path skips with a logged warning. Counts still computed — only qualitative drops.\n- New table missing during a partial deploy (race): query returns empty, route falls back to current behavior (returns counts only, qualitative arrays empty). Documented in `recap.ts` comment.\n- Backfill interrupted: re-runnable from scratch (idempotent).\n\n## 7. Testing & validation\n\n- **Unit tests** for the new SQL functions in `planetscale/checkpoints.test.ts` — three cases each (empty, single-checkpoint, multi-checkpoint).\n- **Route tests** in existing `recap.test.ts` — extend to assert the new query shape and that `Promise.all` is in use.\n- **Perf validation** via the testing tiers we discussed: `wrangler dev --remote` first, then PR preview deploy with PlanetScale schema branch, time `--90` against prod baseline.\n- **Accuracy validation** via the same `sampling-experiment.py` harness — diff Variant 3 output vs current production for the same window. Should be **identical** within rounding (counts) and **set-equal** for top-5 labels/skills (we have exact aggregation now).\n- **Decision gate:** Variant 3 must measure <1.5s for `--90` on PR preview before merge. Otherwise re-evaluate.\n\n## 8. Rollout\n\n1. Schema migration → deploy to PlanetScale main via deploy request\n2. Worker write path (analysis-queue updates) → deploy first so new analyses populate facets in real time\n3. Backfill script run against prod → populates historical data (one-time)\n4. Worker read path switch → queries facets table\n5. Tier 1 (CLI) ships separately on `entireio/cli#1015` — no dependency\n\nOrder matters: write path before read path so facets table is never queried while empty for new data.\n\n---\n\nAnything to revise before I write this up as a spec doc and commit it?"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2200,"cache_read_input_tokens":558975,"output_tokens":2960,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2200,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":6,"output_tokens":2960,"cache_read_input_tokens":558975,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2200,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2200},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CaWHoTtndBW8bNF6f9gxK","type":"assistant","uuid":"8e8f9279-2474-40a3-8f84-15640cb42199","timestamp":"2026-04-28T14:01:29.095Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/entire-activity","sessionId":"a654b6ca-4957-4d7c-8c99-62db313ff0a0","version":"2.1.119","gitBranch":"entire-activity"}
