         INT UNSIGNED  NOT NULL,\n      created_at    TIMESTAMP     NOT NULL DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,\n      PRIMARY KEY (repo_id, checkpoint_id, name),\n      KEY by_repo_name (repo_id, name)\n    ) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb4 COLLATE=utf8mb4_unicode_ci\n  `.execute(db)\n}\n\nexport async function down(db: Kysely<unknown>): Promise<void> {\n  await sql`DROP TABLE repo_checkpoint_analysis_tool_mix`.execute(db)\n  await sql`DROP TABLE repo_checkpoint_analysis_skills`.execute(db)\n  await sql`DROP TABLE repo_checkpoint_analysis_labels`.execute(db)\n}\n```\n\nNote: `repo_id` BINARY(16) and `checkpoint_id` VARBINARY(64) match the existing `repo_checkpoint_analyses` column types — confirm by `grep 'repo_id\\|checkpoint_id' api/db/migrations/*create*analyses*.ts`.\n\n- [ ] **Step 3:** Run the migration against the local Docker MySQL\n\n```bash\ncd api\nmise run api-db-start  # ensure local MySQL is up\npnpm exec tsx scripts/migrate.ts\n```\n\nExpected: `Migration 20260428100000_add_analysis_facet_tables: success` (or whatever the migration runner outputs; check by tailing).\n\n- [ ] **Step 4:** Verify the tables exist\n\n```bash\ndocker exec -i $(docker ps -qf name=mysql) mysql -uentire -pentire entire -e \"SHOW TABLES LIKE '%analysis%'\"\n```\n\nExpected: rows include `repo_checkpoint_analyses`, `repo_checkpoint_analysis_labels`, `repo_checkpoint_analysis_skills`, `repo_checkpoint_analysis_tool_mix`.\n\n- [ ] **Step 5:** Regenerate kysely schema types\n\n```bash\npnpm --dir api run db:codegen\n```\n\nExpected: `api/db/schema.ts` updated. Diff should show three new exported interfaces (`RepoCheckpointAnalysisLabels`, `RepoCheckpointAnalysisSkills`, `RepoCheckpointAnalysisToolMix`) and three additions to the `DB` table map.\n\n- [ ] **Step 6:** Verify no other diffs leaked into schema.ts\n\n```bash\ngit diff api/db/schema.ts\n```\n\nExpected: only the three new interfaces + the three new keys in the `DB` interface. No edits to existing tables.\n\n- [ ] **Step 7