{"parentUuid":"42657ed3-e9ed-4792-97ed-32550fbece28","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01Q9aMTUhSv8G181XB22NhWs","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01MktTGWFQgmGbhxFXW5qMXG","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/entire-activity/docs/superpowers/plans/2026-04-28-recap-perf-and-accuracy.md","content":"# Recap Perf + Accuracy Implementation Plan\n\n> **For agentic workers:** REQUIRED: Use superpowers:subagent-driven-development (if subagents available) or superpowers:executing-plans to implement this plan. Steps use checkbox (`- [ ]`) syntax for tracking.\n\n**Goal:** Improve `/me/recap` latency across **all ranges** (`--day` / `--week` / `--month` / `--90`) without sacrificing accuracy. The `--90` case is the hardest and serves as the validation gate; the same architectural fix proportionally speeds up the shorter ranges. Pair with a CLI client-side cache so subsequent in-session range toggles feel instant (<50ms).\n\n**Architecture:**\n- **Tier 1 (CLI)**: parallel prefetch + cache-clear-on-miss in the recap TUI — already implemented in worktree, just needs commit + push.\n- **Tier 2 (server)**: denormalize qualitative facets (labels, skills, tool-mix) out of `analysis_json` into three small join tables (`repo_checkpoint_analysis_labels`, `_skills`, `_tool_mix`). Replaces the route's `mergeAnalysesInto` JS aggregator (which fetches 1000+ analysis JSON blobs and parses them) with SQL `GROUP BY` queries against the facet tables. Returns ~5-10 rows of pre-aggregated counts per qualitative dimension regardless of input set size.\n\n**Tech Stack:** Cloudflare Workers (Hono), PlanetScale (Vitess + MySQL), Kysely query builder, Vitest for unit tests, TypeScript on the server side. Go (cobra + bubbletea) on the CLI side.\n\n**Repos affected:**\n- `entirehq/entire.io` (`feat/me-recap-endpoint` branch, PR #1604) — server work\n- `entireio/cli` (`entire-activity` branch, PR #1015) — Tier 1 commit\n\n**Success criteria (per range, prod-equivalent measurement on PR preview deploy):**\n\n| Range | Current prod estimate | Target after Tier 2 |\n|---|---|---|\n| `--day` | ~1s | **<300ms** |\n| `--week` | ~2s | **<500ms** |\n| `--month` | ~2-3s | **<700ms** |\n| `--90` | ~2-5s | **<1.5s** |\n\nPlus: subsequent toggles in the same TUI session render in **<50ms** via Tier 1 cache.\n\n---\n\n## Chunk 0: CLI Tier 1 (commit existing code)\n\nThe TUI prefetch + cache-clear-on-miss code is already implemented in the CLI worktree but uncommitted. This chunk just lands it.\n\n### Task 0.1: Verify the working-tree code builds clean\n\n**Files:**\n- Verify: `cmd/entire/cli/recap/tui.go` (already modified locally)\n- Verify: `cmd/entire/cli/recap.go`\n- Verify: `cmd/entire/cli/recap/recap_view.go`\n- Verify: `cmd/entire/cli/recap/tui_test.go`\n\n- [ ] **Step 1:** Switch to the CLI worktree and confirm what's modified\n\n```bash\ncd /Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/entire-activity\ngit status --short\n```\n\nExpected: only the 4 files above show modified. Untracked screenshots in `docs/` are fine. If `cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint/committed.go` or `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/manual_commit_condensation.go` show modified, that's the gofmt-strips-nolint regression — revert them with `git checkout HEAD -- <files>` before proceeding.\n\n- [ ] **Step 2:** Build to confirm no compile errors\n\n```bash\ngo build ./cmd/entire/...\n```\n\nExpected: no output, exit 0.\n\n- [ ] **Step 3:** Run recap unit tests\n\n```bash\ngo test ./cmd/entire/cli/recap/...\n```\n\nExpected: `ok  github.com/entireio/cli/cmd/entire/cli/recap  <time>s`.\n\n- [ ] **Step 4:** Run vet\n\n```bash\ngo vet ./cmd/entire/...\n```\n\nExpected: no output.\n\n### Task 0.2: Commit + push Tier 1\n\n- [ ] **Step 1:** Stage only the four intended files\n\n```bash\ngit add cmd/entire/cli/recap/tui.go cmd/entire/cli/recap.go cmd/entire/cli/recap/recap_view.go cmd/entire/cli/recap/tui_test.go\ngit status --short\n```\n\nExpected: 4 files staged (`M`), nothing else.\n\n- [ ] **Step 2:** Commit\n\n```bash\ngit commit -m \"$(cat <<'EOF'\nperf(recap): prefetch all ranges in parallel + clear stale data on miss\n\nRange toggles (d/w/m/4) used to either show frozen day-1 data (server\nfields cached forever) or display the previous range's numbers under\nthe new range's title (after we added refetch but before we cleared\nstale fields). This wires the TUI through a proper cache:\n\n- On startup, seed cache[initialRange] with the synchronous fetch's\n  payload, then fire prefetches for the other 3 ranges in parallel via\n  tea.Batch. After ~1-5s background round-trip every range toggle is\n  a cache hit.\n- On range toggle: cache hit -> swap data, instant render. Cache miss\n  with no in-flight fetch -> clear server fields (so we don't display\n  the previous range's numbers under the new title), mark loading,\n  fire the fetch. Cache miss with in-flight fetch -> mark loading and\n  wait for the existing reply.\n- Active days now reads from server daily counts when present, matching\n  the dashboard cross-worktree count instead of undercounting from\n  local sessions.\n\nPairs with entirehq/entire.io#1604 server-side perf work.\nEOF\n)\"\n```\n\nExpected: `[entire-activity <hash>] perf(recap): prefetch all ranges in parallel + clear stale data on miss`.\n\n- [ ] **Step 3:** Push to origin\n\n```bash\ngit push origin entire-activity\n```\n\nExpected: `<old>..<new>  entire-activity -> entire-activity`. Ignore the `entire/checkpoints/v1 non-fast-forward` warning.\n\n- [ ] **Step 4:** Confirm CI is running\n\n```bash\ngh pr checks 1015 --watch\n```\n\nWait until all checks pass (~5 min). Critical ones: `lint`, `test-core`, `test-canary`.\n\n---\n\n## Chunk 1: Schema migration\n\nSwitch to the entire.io worktree for everything below.\n\n### Task 1.1: Write the migration\n\n**Files:**\n- Create: `api/db/migrations/20260428100000_add_analysis_facet_tables.ts`\n- Modify: `api/db/schema.ts` (auto-generated via codegen)\n\n- [ ] **Step 1:** Switch to the api worktree and confirm clean tree\n\n```bash\ncd /Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/entire.io/.worktrees/recap-endpoint\ngit status\n```\n\nExpected: `On branch feat/me-recap-endpoint, working tree clean`. If `api/src/routes/recap.ts` shows modified (the perf timing logs from earlier), revert with `git checkout HEAD -- api/src/routes/recap.ts`.\n\n- [ ] **Step 2:** Confirm column types of the existing `repo_checkpoint_analyses` table to match conventions\n\n```bash\ngrep -A 5 'CREATE TABLE.*repo_checkpoint_analyses' api/db/migrations/*.ts | head -20\n```\n\nNote the exact types of `repo_id` and `checkpoint_id` columns.\n\n- [ ] **Step 3:** Create the migration file with the body below. Use the filename `20260428100000_add_analysis_facet_tables.ts` (timestamp matches today, sorts after the most recent existing migration which is `20260427120000_add_gh_pr_id.ts`).\n\n```typescript\nimport { type Kysely, sql } from \"kysely\"\n\n// Three tables denormalize qualitative aggregates out of repo_checkpoint_analyses.analysis_json\n// so /me/recap can GROUP BY in SQL instead of fetching 1000+ rows of full JSON blobs and\n// aggregating in JS. All three share the same shape so the route handler uses one query\n// template against three tables.\n//\n// See docs/superpowers/plans/2026-04-28-recap-perf-and-accuracy.md.\n\nexport async function up(db: Kysely<unknown>): Promise<void> {\n  await sql`\n    CREATE TABLE repo_checkpoint_analysis_labels (\n      repo_id       BINARY(16)    NOT NULL,\n      checkpoint_id VARBINARY(64) NOT NULL,\n      name          VARCHAR(64)   NOT NULL,\n      count         INT UNSIGNED  NOT NULL,\n      created_at    TIMESTAMP     NOT NULL DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,\n      PRIMARY KEY (repo_id, checkpoint_id, name),\n      KEY by_repo_name (repo_id, name)\n    ) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf