{"parentUuid":"65ba5dd6-25da-4779-87e5-01818676f35e","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"b1809b1c-e97c-49cf-aee5-e2f5cf0690a4","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MktTGWFQgmGbhxFXW5qMXG","type":"tool_result","content":"File created successfully at: /Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/entire-activity/docs/superpowers/plans/2026-04-28-recap-perf-and-accuracy.md"}]},"uuid":"4908cf9e-3720-417b-be21-a74bd507d99d","timestamp":"2026-04-28T14:29:30.512Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"create","filePath":"/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/entire-activity/docs/superpowers/plans/2026-04-28-recap-perf-and-accuracy.md","content":"# Recap Perf + Accuracy Implementation Plan\n\n> **For agentic workers:** REQUIRED: Use superpowers:subagent-driven-development (if subagents available) or superpowers:executing-plans to implement this plan. Steps use checkbox (`- [ ]`) syntax for tracking.\n\n**Goal:** Improve `/me/recap` latency across **all ranges** (`--day` / `--week` / `--month` / `--90`) without sacrificing accuracy. The `--90` case is the hardest and serves as the validation gate; the same architectural fix proportionally speeds up the shorter ranges. Pair with a CLI client-side cache so subsequent in-session range toggles feel instant (<50ms).\n\n**Architecture:**\n- **Tier 1 (CLI)**: parallel prefetch + cache-clear-on-miss in the recap TUI — already implemented in worktree, just needs commit + push.\n- **Tier 2 (server)**: denormalize qualitative facets (labels, skills, tool-mix) out of `analysis_json` into three small join tables (`repo_checkpoint_analysis_labels`, `_skills`, `_tool_mix`). Replaces the route's `mergeAnalysesInto` JS aggregator (which fetches 1000+ analysis JSON blobs and parses them) with SQL `GROUP BY` queries against the facet tables. Returns ~5-10 rows of pre-aggregated counts per qualitative dimension regardless of input set size.\n\n**Tech Stack:** Cloudflare Workers (Hono), PlanetScale (Vitess + MySQL), Kysely query builder, Vitest for unit tests, TypeScript on the server side. Go (cobra + bubbletea) on the CLI side.\n\n**Repos affected:**\n- `entirehq/entire.io` (`feat/me-recap-endpoint` branch, PR #1604) — server work\n- `entireio/cli` (`entire-activity` branch, PR #1015) — Tier 1 commit\n\n**Success criteria (per range, prod-equivalent measurement on PR preview deploy):**\n\n| Range | Current prod estimate | Target after Tier 2 |\n|---|---|---|\n| `--day` | ~1s | **<300ms** |\n| `--week` | ~2s | **<500ms** |\n| `--month` | ~2-3s | **<700ms** |\n| `--90` | ~2-5s | **<1.5s** |\n\nPlus: subsequent toggles in the same TUI session render in **<50ms** via Tier 1 cache.\n\n---\n\n## Chunk 0: CLI Tier 1 (commit existing code)\n\nThe TUI prefetch + cache-clear-on-miss code is already implemented in the CLI worktree but uncommitted. This chunk just lands it.\n\n### Task 0.1: Verify the working-tree code builds clean\n\n**Files:**\n- Verify: `cmd/entire/cli/recap/tui.go` (already modified locally)\n- Verify: `cmd/entire/cli/recap.go`\n- Verify: `cmd/entire/cli/recap/recap_view.go`\n- Verify: `cmd/entire/cli/recap/tui_test.go`\n\n- [ ] **Step 1:** Switch to the CLI worktree and confirm what's modified\n\n```bash\ncd /Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/entire-activity\ngit status --short\n```\n\nExpected: only the 4 files above show modified. Untracked screenshots in `docs/` are fine. If `cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint/committed.go` or `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/manual_commit_condensation.go` show modified, that's the gofmt-strips-nolint regression — revert them with `git checkout HEAD -- <files>` before proceeding.\n\n- [ ] **Step 2:** Build to confirm no compile errors\n\n```bash\ngo build ./cmd/entire/...\n```\n\nExpected: no output, exit 0.\n\n- [ ] **Step 3:** Run recap unit tests\n\n```bash\ngo test ./cmd/entire/cli/recap/...\n```\n\nExpected: `ok  github.com/entireio/cli/cmd/entire/cli/recap  <time>s`.\n\n- [ ] **Step 4:** Run vet\n\n```bash\ngo vet ./cmd/entire/...\n```\n\nExpected: no output.\n\n### Task 0.2: Commit + push Tier 1\n\n- [ ] **Step 1:** Stage only the four intended files\n\n```bash\ngit add cmd/entire/cli/recap/tui.go cmd/entire/cli/recap.go cmd/entire/cli/recap/recap_view.go cmd/entire/cli/recap/tui_test.go\ngit status --short\n```\n\nExpected: 4 files staged (`M`), nothing else.\n\n- [ ] **Step 2:** Commit\n\n```bash\ngit commit -m \"$(cat <<'EOF'\nperf(recap): prefetch all ranges in parallel + clear stale data on miss\n\nRange toggles (d/w/m/4) used to either show frozen day-1 data (server\nfields cached forever) or display the previous range's numbers under\nthe new range's title (after we added refetch but before we cleared\nstale fields). This wires the TUI through a proper cache:\n\n- On startup, seed cache[initialRange] with the synchronous fetch's\n  payload, then fire prefetches for the other 3 ranges in parallel via\n  tea.Batch. After ~1-5s background round-trip every range toggle is\n  a cache hit.\n- On range toggle: cache hit -> swap data, instant render. Cache miss\n  with no in-flight fetch -> clear server fields (so we don't display\n  the previous range's numbers under the new title), mark loading,\n  fire the fetch. Cache miss with in-flight fetch -> mark loading and\n  wait for the existing reply.\n- Active days now reads from server daily counts when present, matching\n  the dashboard cross-worktree count instead of undercounting from\n  local sessions.\n\nPairs with entirehq/entire.io#1604 server-side perf work.\nEOF\n)\"\n```\n\nExpected: `[entire-activity <hash>] perf(recap): prefetch all ranges in parallel + clear stale data on miss`.\n\n- [ ] **Step 3:** Push to origin\n\n```bash\ngit push origin entire-activity\n```\n\nExpected: `<old>..<new>  entire-activity -> entire-activity`. Ignore the `entire/checkpoints/v1 non-fast-forward` warning.\n\n- [ ] **Step 4:** Confirm CI is running\n\n```bash\ngh pr checks 1015 --watch\n```\n\nWait until all checks pass (~5 min). Critical ones: `lint`, `test-core`, `test-canary`.\n\n---\n\n## Chunk 1: Schema migration\n\nSwitch to the entire.io worktree for everything below.\n\n### Task 1.1: Write the migration\n\n**Files:**\n- Create: `api/db/migrations/20260428100000_add_analysis_facet_tables.ts`\n- Modify: `api/db/schema.ts` (auto-generated via codegen)\n\n- [ ] **Step 1:** Switch to the api worktree and confirm clean tree\n\n```bash\ncd /Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/entire.io/.worktrees/recap-endpoint\ngit status\n```\n\nExpected: `On branch feat/me-recap-endpoint, working tree clean`. If `api/src/routes/recap.ts` shows modified (the perf timing logs from earlier), revert with `git checkout HEAD -- api/src/routes/recap.ts`.\n\n- [ ] **Step 2:** Confirm column types of the existing `repo_checkpoint_analyses` table to match conventions\n\n```bash\ngrep -A 5 'CREATE TABLE.*repo_checkpoint_analyses' api/db/migrations/*.ts | head -20\n```\n\nNote the exact types of `repo_id` and `checkpoint_id` columns.\n\n- [ ] **Step 3:** Create the migration file with the body below. Use the filename `20260428100000_add_analysis_facet_tables.ts` (timestamp matches today, sorts after the most recent existing migration which is `20260427120000_add_gh_pr_id.ts`).\n\n```typescript\nimport { type Kysely, sql } from \"kysely\"\n\n// Three tables denormalize qualitative aggregates out of repo_checkpoint_analyses.analysis_json\n// so /me/recap can GROUP BY in SQL instead of fetching 1000+ rows of full JSON blobs and\n// aggregating in JS. All three share the same shape so the route handler uses one query\n// template against three tables.\n//\n// See docs/superpowers/plans/2026-04-28-recap-perf-and-accuracy.md.\n\nexport async function up(db: Kysely<unknown>): Promise<void> {\n  await sql`\n    CREATE TABLE repo_checkpoint_analysis_labels (\n      repo_id       BINARY(16)    NOT NULL,\n      checkpoint_id VARBINARY(64) NOT NULL,\n      name          VARCHAR(64)   NOT NULL,\n      count         INT UNSIGNED  NOT NULL,\n      created_at    TIMESTAMP     NOT NULL DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,\n      PRIMARY KEY (repo_id, checkpoint_id, name),\n      KEY by_repo_name (repo_id, name)\n    ) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb4 COLLATE=utf8mb4_unicode_ci\n  `.execute(db)\n\n  await sql`\n    CREATE TABLE repo_checkpoint_analysis_skills (\n      repo_id       BINARY(16)    NOT NULL,\n      checkpoint_id VARBINARY(64) NOT NULL,\n      name          VARCHAR(64)   NOT NULL,\n      count         INT UNSIGNED  NOT NULL,\n      created_at    TIMESTAMP     NOT NULL DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,\n      PRIMARY KEY (repo_id, checkpoint_id, name),\n      KEY by_repo_name (repo_id, name)\n    ) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb4 COLLATE=utf8mb4_unicode_ci\n  `.execute(db)\n\n  await sql`\n    CREATE TABLE repo_checkpoint_analysis_tool_mix (\n      repo_id       BINARY(16)    NOT NULL,\n      checkpoint_id VARBINARY(64) NOT NULL,\n      name          VARCHAR(32)   NOT NULL,\n      count         INT UNSIGNED  NOT NULL,\n      created_at    TIMESTAMP     NOT NULL DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,\n      PRIMARY KEY (repo_id, checkpoint_id, name),\n      KEY by_repo_name (repo_id, name)\n    ) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb4 COLLATE=utf8mb4_unicode_ci\n  `.execute(db)\n}\n\nexport async function down(db: Kysely<unknown>): Promise<void> {\n  await sql`DROP TABLE repo_checkpoint_analysis_tool_mix`.execute(db)\n  await sql`DROP TABLE repo_checkpoint_analysis_skills`.execute(db)\n  await sql`DROP TABLE repo_checkpoint_analysis_labels`.execute(db)\n}\n```\n\nIf the actual column types of `repo_checkpoint_analyses` differ from `BINARY(16)` / `VARBINARY(64)`, adjust the new migration to match before running.\n\n- [ ] **Step 4:** Run the migration against the local Docker MySQL\n\n```bash\ncd api\nmise run api-db-start\npnpm exec tsx scripts/migrate.ts\n```\n\nExpected: success log entry for `20260428100000_add_analysis_facet_tables`.\n\n- [ ] **Step 5:** Verify the tables exist\n\n```bash\ndocker exec -i $(docker ps -qf name=mysql) mysql -uentire -pentire entire -e \"SHOW TABLES LIKE 'repo_checkpoint_analysis_%'\"\n```\n\nExpected: 4 rows including the existing `repo_checkpoint_analyses` and the 3 new tables.\n\n- [ ] **Step 6:** Regenerate Kysely schema types\n\n```bash\npnpm --dir api run db:codegen\n```\n\nExpected: `api/db/schema.ts` updated with three new exported interfaces (`RepoCheckpointAnalysisLabels`, `RepoCheckpointAnalysisSkills`, `RepoCheckpointAnalysisToolMix`) and three additions to the `DB` table map.\n\n- [ ] **Step 7:** Verify no other diffs leaked into schema.ts\n\n```bash\ngit diff api/db/schema.ts\n```\n\nExpected: only additions for the three new tables.\n\n- [ ] **Step 8:** Commit\n\n```bash\ngit add api/db/migrations/20260428100000_add_analysis_facet_tables.ts api/db/schema.ts\ngit commit -m \"feat(recap): add denormalized analysis facet tables\n\nThree tables for labels, skills, and tool-mix aggregates that today\nlive as JSON blobs inside repo_checkpoint_analyses.analysis_json.\nIdentical schema across all three: (repo_id, checkpoint_id, name, count)\nwith PK and a (repo_id, name) index for cross-checkpoint aggregation.\n\nEmpty until the analysis-queue worker writes to them (next chunk) and\nthe backfill script populates historical rows.\"\n```\n\n---\n\n## Chunk 2: Database namespace methods\n\n### Task 2.1: Extend AnalysesNamespace types in db-types.ts\n\n**Files:**\n- Modify: `api/src/lib/db/db-types.ts`\n\n- [ ] **Step 1:** Open `db-types.ts` and locate the `AnalysesNamespace` interface (around line 121, the line `getByCheckpointIds(repoId, checkpointIds)` is in it).\n\n- [ ] **Step 2:** Insert the following new types immediately above `AnalysesNamespace`:\n\n```typescript\nexport type AnalysisFacetKind = \"labels\" | \"skills\" | \"tool_mix\"\n\nexport interface AnalysisFacetCount {\n  name: string\n  count: number\n}\n\nexport interface AnalysisFacetCheckpointRef {\n  repo_id: string\n  checkpoint_id: string\n}\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 3:** Add three method signatures inside the `AnalysesNamespace` interface (alongside the existing `getByCheckpointIds`):\n\n```typescript\n  // Replace all facet rows for a checkpoint atomically (DELETE then INSERT).\n  // Idempotent — re-running with the same inputs yields the same final state.\n  upsertFacets(\n    repoId: string,\n    checkpointId: string,\n    labels: AnalysisFacetCount[],\n    skills: AnalysisFacetCount[],\n    toolMix: AnalysisFacetCount[],\n  ): Promise<void>\n\n  // SUM(count) GROUP BY name across the given checkpoint set, for one facet kind.\n  // Returns rows sorted by total descending. Empty input returns an empty array.\n  aggregateFacetsByCheckpointSet(\n    kind: AnalysisFacetKind,\n    checkpoints: AnalysisFacetCheckpointRef[],\n  ): Promise<Array<{ name: string; total: number }>>\n\n  // Per-agent aggregate for the given checkpoint set, returning per-agent\n  // label/skill/toolMix rollups in a single helper. Built on top of\n  // aggregateFacetsByCheckpointSet but groups by agent first (agent is supplied\n  // by the caller because it lives on repo_checkpoints, not on the facet tables).\n  aggregateFacetsByAgent(\n    checkpoints: Array<{ repo_id: string; checkpoint_id: string; agent: string | null }>,\n  ): Promise<\n    Map<\n      string,\n      {\n        labels: AnalysisFacetCount[]\n        skills: AnalysisFacetCount[]\n        toolMix: AnalysisFacetCount[]\n      }\n    >\n  >\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 4:** `pnpm --dir api typecheck` — should fail. The implementations don't exist yet. Expected red.\n\n### Task 2.2: Test-first — upsertFacets writes correct rows\n\n**Files:**\n- Create: `api/src/lib/planetscale/analyses-facets.test.ts`\n\n- [ ] **Step 1:** Inspect the existing `analyses.test.ts` (or peer test file) to learn how the test database is set up.\n\n```bash\nls api/src/lib/planetscale/*.test.ts\nhead -40 api/src/lib/planetscale/checkpoints.test.ts 2>/dev/null\n```\n\nMirror that pattern in the new test file.\n\n- [ ] **Step 2:** Write the failing test with this content (adjust imports to match the discovered test-db helper):\n\n```typescript\nimport { afterEach, beforeEach, describe, expect, it } from \"vitest\"\nimport type { Kysely } from \"kysely\"\n\nimport type { DB } from \"../../../db/schema\"\nimport { setupTestDb, teardownTestDb } from \"../../../test-utils/db\" // adjust path\nimport { createAnalysesNamespace } from \"./analyses\"\n\ndescribe(\"upsertFacets\", () => {\n  let db: Kysely<DB>\n\n  beforeEach(async () => {\n    db = await setupTestDb()\n  })\n\n  afterEach(async () => {\n    await teardownTestDb(db)\n  })\n\n  it(\"inserts label, skill, and tool-mix rows\", async () => {\n    const ns = createAnalysesNamespace(db)\n    const repoId = \"00000000000000000000000000000001\"\n    const cpId = \"cp-test-1\"\n\n    await ns.upsertFacets(\n      repoId,\n      cpId,\n      [{ name: \"bug_fix\", count: 2 }, { name: \"refactor\", count: 1 }],\n      [{ name: \"code-review\", count: 3 }],\n      [{ name: \"shell\", count: 5 }, { name: \"fileOps\", count: 7 }],\n    )\n\n    const labels = await db\n      .selectFrom(\"repo_checkpoint_analysis_labels\")\n      .where(\"repo_id\", \"=\", repoId)\n      .where(\"checkpoint_id\", \"=\", cpId)\n      .selectAll()\n      .execute()\n\n    expect(labels).toHaveLength(2)\n    expect(labels.map((l) => l.name).sort()).toEqual([\"bug_fix\", \"refactor\"])\n  })\n\n  it(\"is idempotent — re-running replaces prior rows\", async () => {\n    const ns = createAnalysesNamespace(db)\n    const repoId = \"00000000000000000000000000000002\"\n    const cpId = \"cp-test-2\"\n\n    await ns.upsertFacets(repoId, cpId, [{ name: \"old\", count: 1 }], [], [])\n    await ns.upsertFacets(repoId, cpId, [{ name: \"new\", count: 1 }], [], [])\n\n    const labels = await db\n      .selectFrom(\"repo_checkpoint_analysis_labels\")\n      .where(\"repo_id\", \"=\", repoId)\n      .where(\"