tireio/cli` (`entire-activity` branch, PR #1015) — Tier 1 commit\n\n**Success criteria (per range, prod-equivalent measurement on PR preview deploy):**\n\n| Range | Current prod estimate | Target after Tier 2 |\n|---|---|---|\n| `--day` | ~1s | **<300ms** |\n| `--week` | ~2s | **<500ms** |\n| `--month` | ~2-3s | **<700ms** |\n| `--90` | ~2-5s | **<1.5s** |\n\nPlus: subsequent toggles in the same TUI session render in **<50ms** via Tier 1 cache.\n\n---\n\n## Prerequisites (read once before starting)\n\nThese are pinned answers to facts every chunk relies on. If you find them stale, fix the prereqs first before continuing — silent drift here cascades.\n\n- **CLI worktree:** `/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/entire-activity` (branch `entire-activity`)\n- **Server worktree:** `/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/entire.io/.worktrees/recap-endpoint` (branch `feat/me-recap-endpoint`)\n- **DB types import path:** `../../../db/types` (from `api/src/lib/planetscale/`)\n- **Kysely version:** `^0.28.15` — uses `eb` for expression builder (NOT the deprecated `cmpr`)\n- **Test pattern:** integration tests against real local MySQL via helpers in `api/test/planetscale/mysql-test-client.ts`. Mirror `api/src/lib/planetscale/analyses.test.ts` exactly:\n\n```typescript\nimport { describe, it, expect, beforeAll, beforeEach, afterAll } from \"vitest\"\nimport {\n  getTestKysely, resetMySQLDatabase, destroyTestKysely,\n  createTestRepo, createTestCheckpoint, getTestDbClient,\n} from \"../../../test/planetscale/mysql-test-client\"\nimport type { AnalysesNamespace } from \"../db/db-types\"\n\nlet analyses: AnalysesNamespace\nlet repoId: string\nlet checkpointId: string\n\nbeforeAll(async () => {\n  const db = getTestKysely()\n  await resetMySQLDatabase(db)\n  analyses = getTestDbClient(db).analyses\n})\n\nbeforeEach(async () => {\n  const db = getTestKysely()\n  await resetMySQLDatabase(db)\n  const repo = await createTestRepo(db)\n  repoId = repo.id\n  const cp = await createTestCheckpoint(db, repoId, { checkpoint_id: \"cp-test-001\" })\n  checkpointId = cp.checkpoint_id\n})\n\nafterAll(async () => {\n  await destroyTestKysely()\n})\n```\n\n- **Existing `repo_checkpoint_analyses` column types:** `repo_id char(36)`, `checkpoint_id varchar(255)`. The new facet tables MUST match (`char(36)` / `varchar(255)`) so foreign-key-style joins line up.\n- **Migration style:** Kysely schema builder (`db.schema.createTable(...).addColumn(...)`), NOT raw SQL. See `api/db/migrations/20260410000000_add_repo_checkpoint_analyses.ts` as the canonical template.\n- **Persist function in analysis-queue:** `db.analyses.markComplete(...)` is called at `api/src/lib/analysis-queue.ts:722`. Wire `upsertFacets` immediately after that call, in the same function.\n- **Backfill template:** mirror `api/scripts/backfill-search.ts` for imports, db setup, and the `DATABASE_URL` env var pattern. Specifically, the connection setup is:\n\n```typescript\nimport { Kysely, MysqlDialect } from \"kysely\"\nimport { createPool } from \"mysql2\"\nimport type { DB } from \"../db/types\"\n\nconst url = process.env.DATABASE_URL ?? \"REDACTED\"\nconst pool = createPool({ uri: url })\nconst db = new Kysely<DB>({ dialect: new MysqlDialect({ pool }) })\n```\n\n- **`dev:remote` script confirmed in `api/package.json`:** `\"dev:remote\": \"wrangler dev --remote\"` — runs the worker on real Cloudflare infrastructure against the bound hyperdrive (production-equivalent perf).\n- **PlanetScale tuple-IN syntax verified working** on the entire-io keyspace via direct mysql2 test (Apr 28 2026). `WHERE (repo_id, checkpoint_id) IN ((?,?), (?,?))` uses the composite primary key per `EXPLAIN`. No fallback needed.\n- **`count` is a reserved word in some MySQL contexts.** Quote it in raw SQL fragments using `` sql.ref('count') `` or backticks (`` `count` ``) — never bare `count` inside a `sql\\`\\`` template.\n\n---\n\n## Chunk 0: CLI Tier 1 (commit existing code)\n\