ggregates overlays per-agent facet aggregates (computed in\n// SQL via aggregateFacetsByAgent) onto the per-agent count rollups. Replaces\n// the previous JS-side mergeAnalysesInto + per-checkpoint analysis_json fetch.\n//\n// AgentAggregate.toolMix has a fixed key set (shell/fileOps/search/mcp/agent/\n// other). We only overwrite known keys so stray facet names from a malformed\n// analysis can't pollute the response shape.\nfunction mergeFacetsIntoAggregates(\n  byAgent: Record<string, AgentAggregate>,\n  facets: Map<string, AnalysisFacetsByAgent>,\n): void {\n  const toolMixKeys = new Set([\"shell\", \"fileOps\", \"search\", \"mcp\", \"agent\", \"other\"])\n  for (const [agent, f] of facets) {\n    const agg = byAgent[agent]\n    if (!agg) continue\n    agg.labels = f.labels.map((l) => ({ label: l.name, count: l.count }))\n    agg.skills = f.skills.map((s) => ({ skill: s.name, count: s.count }))\n    for (const t of f.toolMix) {\n      if (toolMixKeys.has(t.name)) {\n        ;(agg.toolMix as Record<string, number>)[t.name] = t.count\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\nImport `AnalysisFacetsByAgent` from the types module:\n\n```typescript\nimport type { AnalysisFacetsByAgent } from \"../lib/db/db-types\"\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 4:** Run the existing route tests to confirm nothing regressed\n\n```bash\npnpm --dir api test:unit -- recap.test\n```\n\nExpected: all pass (the legacy path is still intact behind the flag).\n\n- [ ] **Step 5:** Run typecheck + format\n\n```bash\npnpm --dir api typecheck\npnpm format:check\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 6:** Commit\n\n```bash\ngit add api/src/routes/recap.ts\ngit commit -m \"perf(recap): aggregate qualitative facets in SQL (feature-flagged)\n\nUSE_FACET_AGGREGATOR=true routes through the new\ndb.analyses.aggregateFacetsByAgent (SQL GROUP BY against the three\nfacet tables); =false retains the legacy mergeAnalysesInto JS\naggregator. Defaults on for the rollout; flag stays for ~24 hours\npost-deploy as a fast-rollback escape hatch.\n\nReturns ~5-10 rows of pre-aggregated counts per qualitative dimension\ninstead of 1000+ rows of analysis_json blobs. Expected ~5x prod\nlatency improvement on /me/recap?--90; proportional improvements on\nshorter ranges.\"\n```\n\n### Task 5.3: Add a route test for the new aggregator path\n\n**Files:**\n- Modify: `api/src/routes/recap.test.ts`\n\n- [ ] **Step 1:** Read the existing recap.test.ts setup to understand its mock pattern (it uses `vi.mock(\"../lib/db\")` based on the file we wrote earlier).\n\n```bash\nhead -60 api/src/routes/recap.test.ts\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 2:** Extend the existing `vi.mock(\"../lib/db\")` to expose `aggregateFacetsByAgent` as a mock, and add a test asserting the route uses its output.\n\n```typescript\n// In the existing vi.mock, add:\nconst mockAggregateFacetsByAgent = vi.fn()\n\nvi.mock(\"../lib/db\", () => ({\n  getDb: () => ({\n    users: { getWithCache: (...args: unknown[]) => mockGetWithCache(...args) },\n    checkpoints: {\n      getByUser: (...args: unknown[]) => mockGetByUser(...args),\n      getTeamOnUserRepos: (...args: unknown[]) => mockGetTeamOnUserRepos(...args),\n    },\n    analyses: {\n      getByCheckpointIds: (...args: unknown[]) => mockGetByCheckpointIds(...args),\n      aggregateFacetsByAgent: (...args: unknown[]) => mockAggregateFacetsByAgent(...args),\n    },\n  }),\n}))\n\n// In the describe block, before the beforeEach:\nbeforeEach(() => {\n  // ...existing resets...\n  mockAggregateFacetsByAgent.mockResolvedValue(new Map())\n})\n\n// New test:\nit(\"uses aggregateFacetsByAgent output verbatim for team qualitative aggregates\", async () => {\n  mockGetByUser.mockResolvedValue([\n    { repo_id: \"r\", checkpoint_id: \"cp-1\", agent: \"Claude Code\", input_tokens: 100, output_tokens: 50 },\n  ])\n  mockGetTeamOnUserRepos.mockResolvedValue([\n    { repo_id: \"r\", checkpoint_id: \"cp-team-1\", agent: \"Claude Code\", commit_author_github_id: 999, input_tokens: 200, output_tokens: 100 },\n  ])\n  mockAggregateFacetsByAgent\n    .mockResolvedValueOnce(new Map()) // me-side facets — empty for this test\n    .mockResolvedValueOnce(new Map([\n      [\"Claude Code\", {\n        labels:  [{ name: \"bug_fix\",  count: 5 }, { name: \"refactor\", count: 2 }],\n        skills:  [{ name: \"debugging\", count: 3 }],\n        toolMix: [{ name: \"shell\", count: 12 }, { name: \"fileOps\", count: 8 }],\n      }],\n    ]))\n\n  const res = await get(\"/?repo=org/app\")\n  expect(res.status).toBe(200)\n  const body = (await res.json()) as {\n    agents: Record<string, {\n      contributors: {\n        labels: Array<{ label: string; count: number }>\n        skills: Array<{ skill: string; count: number }>\n        toolMix: Record<string, number>\n      } | null\n    }>\n  }\n  expect(body.agents[\"Claude Code\"].contributors!.labels).toEqual([\n    { label: \"bug_fix\", count: 5 },\n    { label: \"refactor\", count: 2 },\n  ])\n  expect(body.agents[\"Claude Code\"].contributors!.skills).toEqual([\n    { skill: \"debugging\", count: 3 },\n  ])\n  expect(body.agents[\"Claude Code\"].contributors!.toolMix.shell).toBe(12)\n})\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 3:** Run\n\n```bash\npnpm --dir api test:unit -- recap.test\n```\n\nExpected: pass.\n\n- [ ] **Step 4:** Commit\n\n```bash\ngit add api/src/routes/recap.test.ts\ngit commit -m \"test(recap): assert route uses aggregateFacetsByAgent output\n\nPins the wiring between the new db method and the response shape so\nthe team qualitative columns can't silently regress.\"\n```\n\n---\n\n## Chunk 6: Local validation\n\n### Task 6.1: Commit the sampling experiment script for portability\n\n**Files:**\n- Create: `api/scripts/perf/sampling-experiment.py`\n\n- [ ] **Step 1:** Move the experimental script (currently at `/tmp/sampling-experiment.py`) into the repo so future plan executors have it:\n\n```bash\nmkdir -p api/scripts/perf\ncp /tmp/sampling-experiment.py api/scripts/perf/sampling-experiment.py 2>/dev/null \\\n  || cat > api/scripts/perf/sampling-experiment.py <<'