{"parentUuid":"2d9e4bbb-d486-4a6c-8ecd-95a23abb56cb","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01Qs3UYqG1idge9JEWt7DMDW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Really fair question. Let me untangle what's actually needed for testing:\n\n`★ Insight ─────────────────────────────────────`\n- **Safe migrations is needed to open a deploy request, not to test.** A deploy request is what merges schema changes into the production `main` branch. We don't need that for testing — we just need our schema applied somewhere with data we can query.\n- **But: PlanetScale schema branches are schema-only by default.** No data clones in. The schema branch is empty. So even if we got our worker pointing at it, perf testing would be meaningless (every query returns instantly because there's nothing to aggregate).\n- **The only way to measure prod-equivalent perf is against production-shape data**, which means deploying the schema to main. That's exactly what safe migrations + deploy request gates.\n`─────────────────────────────────────────────────`\n\n## Honest options at this point\n\n| Option | What you get | Cost |\n|---|---|---|\n| **A) Stop pre-merge perf testing; mark PR ready and let CI + reviewer handle the rest** | Code review + normal merge flow. The deploy itself is when prod perf gets measured (whoever approves the deploy request can verify on staging-equivalent before flipping the flag). | 0 — we're done |\n| **B) Ping a teammate with admin perms** to enable safe migrations + approve the deploy request | Get the prod schema deployed → real perf measurement | Their time + ~30 min |\n| **C) Continue testing locally with real-shape data** | Seed a few thousand fake checkpoints into local Docker, measure | Hours of fake-data setup; numbers still misleading vs prod hyperdrive |\n\n## My recommendation: A — mark PR ready, hand off to review\n\nReasoning:\n- We've already proven functional correctness (2,041 unit tests passi