ently include bot-author checkpoints, dropping the inequality would double-count the user's own checkpoints on the team side. None of these are caught by the route tests because they mock `getTeamOnUserRepos` directly.\n- The `user_repos` join (`checkpoints.ts:1820-1822`) silently scopes the team set to repos the user has access to. If that join is removed, the endpoint leaks team activity from repos the user shouldn't see — a privacy regression. The route-level mocks bypass this entirely.\n\n**2. Error/exception path returns 500 — uncovered. `recap.ts:288-292`.** Criticality 8.\n- No test forces `db.users.getWithCache`, `db.checkpoints.getByUser`, or any of the four DB calls to throw. The 500 branch and `recordSpanError(err)` call are dead from a test-coverage standpoint. A regression that swallows the error or returns 200 with a partial body would not be caught.\n\n**3. 404 path for missing user — uncovered. `recap.ts:191-192`.** Criticality 8.\n- `mockGetWithCache` is only ever set to a valid user in `beforeEach` (`recap.test.ts:81`). There is no test where it returns `null`/`undefined` to verify the 404 with `{error: \"User not found\"}` body and that `getByUser` is *not* subsequently called. Easy to regress into a 500 or null deref.\n\n---\n\n### Important Gaps (5-7)\n\n**4. `aggregateCheckpointsByAgent` null-agent fallback uncovered. `recap.ts:325`.** Criticality 6.\n- `cp.agent ?? \"unknown\"` is the sole bucket for checkpoints with no agent metadata. No test produces a checkpoint with `agent: null`, so a regression that drops the fallback (or renames the bucket) is silent.\n\n**5. `parseRecapWindow` partial-param fallback uncovered. `recap.ts:301-315`.** Criticality 7.\n- Only the both-params-present case is tested (`recap.test.ts:156-165`). All these slip past:\n  - `?since=...` without `until` → must fall back to timeframe (currently the implicit behavior, but no assertion).\n  - `?since=garbage&until=garbage` (NaN dates) → must fall back to timeframe; this is the silent-bug case where invalid input could otherwise produce a window of `Invalid Date` strings reaching the JSON response.\n  - `?limit=99999` with explicit since/until → currently clamped to 1000 inside `parseRecapWindow` but only in the explicit-date branch; behavior under `parseTimeframeParams` differs.\n  - `?limit=-5` or `?limit=abc` → falls through to `500` default. Worth one assertion since it touches user input.\n\n**6. `mergeAnalysesInto` ignores incomplete/malformed JSON — only the `repo_id`-scoping happy path is tested. `recap.ts:404-410`.** Criticality 6.\n- The `status !== \"complete\"` branch (`recap.ts:404`) and the `JSON.parse` `try/catch` are both untested. A regression that propagates malformed analysis JSON would produce a 500 instead of a degraded response. The `recap.test.ts:185-205` test only feeds well-formed `complete` rows.\n\n**7. `mergeAnalysesInto` agent-mismatch branch uncovered. `recap.ts:418-419`.** Criticality 5.\n- `if (!agg) continue` handles the case where an analysis exists for a checkpoint whose agent doesn't appear in `byAgent` (e.g., team-side analysis whose agent isn't in the me set when only team has it). The me/team aggregation is built independently per call, so this branch is unlikely to hit in practice — but it is a silent-skip that warrants one explicit test.\n\n**8. `buildDailyActivity` uncovered. `recap.ts:350-371`.** Criticality 6.\n- No test asserts `daily` structure — empty days produce `count: 0`, days outside the window are dropped, days at the boundary are included. Off-by-one in the loop bound (`cursor <= endDay`) is exactly the kind of bug that ships and goes unnoticed for a release. Also the `commit_date` slicing assumes ISO-8601; non-ISO `commit_date` strings would silently drop.\n\n**9. Team-side aggregation paths uncovered. `recap.ts:226, 235, 274`.** Criticality 7.\n- The \"scopes both queries\" test (`recap.test.ts:102-125`) only checks that arguments are passed correctly. **No test populates `mockGetTeamOnUserRepos` with real checkpoints AND asserts the resulting `agents.<name>.contributors` structure.** This means:\n  - The merge of team analyses into `teamByAgent` is unverified end-to-end (`recap.ts:235`).\n  - The \"agents that appear on either side\" union logic at `recap.ts:269` is uncovered when team has agents the user doesn't.\n  - The `repoParam ? (teamByAgent[name] ?? null) : null` at `recap.ts:274` is uncovered for the case `agent on me side but no team activity for that agent` (the `?? null` branch).\n\n**10. `contributors.totalTokens` / `totalCheckpoints` math uncovered. `recap.ts:261-262`.** Criticality 6.\n- The distinct-users count is asserted at `recap.test.ts:153`, but `totalTokens` and `totalCheckpoints` (sum of me + team) are never asserted. A regression that double-counts or scopes only to one side would slip through.\n\n**11. Empty `teamCheckpoints` with `?repo=` set — partial coverage. `recap.ts:252-264`.** Criticality 5.\n- When `?repo=` is set but the team has zero checkpoints, `contribSummary.distinctUsers` should equal 1 (just the requesting user). No test pins this; the existing `?repo=` test (`recap.test.ts:102`) doesn't read the contributors object.\n\n---\n\n### Test Quality Issues\n\n**12. `mockGetTeamOnUserRepos` doesn't validate the `repoParam ?? undefined` translation. `recap.ts:209, 218`.** Criticality 4.\n- The route passes `repoParam ?? undefined` to `getByUser` but `repoParam` straight to `getTeamOnUserRepos`. Test at `recap.test.ts:109-124` checks both as `\"org/app\"` but never asserts the omitted-repo case for `getByUser` passes `undefined` (not `null`, not `\"\"`). Important since the SQL builder branches on truthiness.\n\n**13. Tests over-mock the DB layer.** Criticality 3.\n- Mocking `getDb` wholesale (`recap.test.ts:23-34`) is fine for handler logic, but it means the contract between handler and DB types (e.g., a future rename of `getTeamOnUserRepos` → something else) isn't caught at the unit level. Acceptable 