on them.\n5. **Untested 500 path** — no test covers `recap.ts:288-292` catch.\n\n### PR #1737 (perf refactor)\n\n6. **Torn-write window between facets and scalars** — `analysis-queue.ts:727-745` calls `upsertFacets` (transactional) then `updateScalarAggregates` (separate UPDATE). If the second fails after the first commits, the row has fresh facets but `transcript_tokens=0`/`files_changed=0`. Worker won't retry because `markComplete` already returned true. Fix: wrap both in a single transaction.\n7. **`mergeFacetsIntoAggregates` silently drops unknown toolMix names** — `recap.ts:506-516` filters by hardcoded `Set` of 6 keys. A new category in the producer disappears silently. Fix: shared constant exported from analysis-queue + warn on drop.\n8. **`USE_FACET_AGGREGATOR=false` is dead code in tests** — flag is hardcoded `const` (not env-gated despite the comment promising \"no redeploy\"). The legacy branch isn't covered by any test, so flipping it during an incident is a leap of faith.\n9. **`upsertFacets` partial-failure rollback unverified** — claim \"consumers never see partial facet rows\" has no test. Add one that forces an INSERT failure and asserts no rows mutated.\n\n## IMPORTANT\n\nPR #1604:\n- OpenAPI 404 description says \"User or repo not found\" — only user 404 is emitted (`recap.ts:174-176`).\n- `Promise.all([mergeAnalysesInto me, mergeAnalysesInto team])` — one team-side failure tanks the whole 500.\n- `getByCheckpointIds` per-repo loop is sequential, no per-repo error context, abort on first throw.\n- Default-coalescing on `?? 0` and `?? []` masks analysis-shape drift.\n- `cp.agent ?? \"unknown\"` magic string differs from `LEGACY_FALLBACK_AGENT_NAME` constant elsewhere.\n\nPR #1737:\n- Backfill `--dry-run` silently ignores `--limit=N` (loop only increments `wouldUpsert`, not `processed`).\n- Backfill catch-all skip swallows infra errors as if they were JSON parse errors — script reports success while skipping 1000s on a PlanetScale flap.\n- Migration