{"parentUuid":"6c1f29d2-1a47-4224-b43e-0e6905853afd","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"edited_text_file","filename":"/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/entire.io/.worktrees/recap-endpoint/api/src/env.ts","snippet":"1\t// Cloudflare Workers environment bindings\n2\t\n3\t/**\n4\t * Type utility to extract required (non-optional) keys from a type.\n5\t */\n6\ttype RequiredKeys<T> = {\n7\t  [K in keyof T]-?: undefined extends T[K] ? never : K\n8\t}[keyof T]\n9\t\n10\t/**\n11\t * All required (non-optional) keys from the Env interface.\n12\t */\n13\ttype RequiredEnvKey = RequiredKeys<Env>\n14\t\n15\t/**\n16\t * List of required environment variables validated at runtime by validateEnv().\n17\t *\n18\t * TypeScript helps keep this list in sync with the Env interface:\n19\t * - `satisfies readonly RequiredEnvKey[]` ensures each entry is a valid required key\n20\t * - The compile-time assertion below errors if any required Env key is missing\n21\t *\n22\t * However, the actual validation happens at runtime since TypeScript types are\n23\t * erased. The validateEnv() function checks that these values are present and\n24\t * non-empty when the worker handles its first request.\n25\t */\n26\tconst REQUIRED_ENV_VARS = [\n27\t  \"ENCRYPTION_KEY\",\n28\t  \"ENTIRE_CACHE\",\n29\t  \"ENVIRONMENT\",\n30\t  \"FRONTEND_BASE_URL\",\n31\t  \"GITHUB_APP_NAME\",\n32\t  \"GITHUB_APP_PRIVATE_KEY\",\n33\t  \"GITHUB_CLIENT_ID\",\n34\t  \"GITHUB_CLIENT_SECRET\",\n35\t  \"GITHUB_WEBHOOK_SECRET\",\n36\t  \"AGENT_RUN_QUEUE\",\n37\t  \"HYPERDRIVE\",\n38\t  \"HYPERDRIVE_BACKGROUND\",\n39\t  \"REPO_SYNC_QUEUE\",\n40\t  \"SESSION_SECRET\",\n41\t  \"USER_REPO_SYNC_QUEUE\",\n42\t  \"WEBHOOK_QUEUE\",\n43\t] as const satisfies readonly RequiredEnvKey[]\n44\t\n45\t// Compile-time check: fails to build if any required Env key is missing from the array above\n46\ttype _MissingKeys = Exclude<RequiredEnvKey, (typeof REQUIRED_ENV_VARS)[number]>\n47\ttype _AssertComplete = [_MissingKey