{"parentUuid":"a470aa08-848f-4144-bc11-4e749567291c","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01WMQTR1GaazJPY2A4gyixF1","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01AjqtKQQNxy7JrEr9DUgcjn","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/entire.io/.worktrees/recap-endpoint && gh pr edit 1737 --repo entirehq/entire.io --body \"$(cat <<'EOF'\n## Summary\n\nFollow-up to #1604. Moves /me/recap qualitative aggregates (labels, skills, MCP servers, tool-mix, transcript tokens, files changed) out of `analysis_json` blobs and into denormalized side tables so the route can `GROUP BY` in SQL instead of fetching 1000+ rows of full JSON blobs and aggregating in JS.\n\n**Stacks on top of #1604** — base is `feat/me-recap-endpoint`. Once #1604 merges, GitHub auto-rebases this onto `main` and the diff shows only the perf-specific delta.\n\n## Why\n\n#1604 ships /me/recap matching the /me/activity pattern (fetch checkpoints + analyses, aggregate in JS). Production-equivalent perf measurements showed `--90` recap took 60s+ on local wrangler dev — the workerd ↔ Node JSON serialization boundary doesn't scale linearly with row count, and we're shipping ~1000 analysis_json blobs per request.\n\nThis PR replaces that with SQL `GROUP BY` against four small denormalized facet tables. Aggregate response size drops from ~1KB-1MB of nested JSON to 5-10 rows of `(name, count)` aggregates per qualitative dimension.\n\n## Architecture\n\n**Schema** — four new tables, identical shape, `(repo_id, checkpoint_id, name, count)` with composite PK and a `(repo_id, name)` index for cross-checkpoint aggregation:\n- `repo_checkpoint_analysis_labels`\n- `repo_checkpoint_analysis_skills`\n- `repo_checkpoint_analysis_tool_mix`\n- `repo_checkpoint_analysis_mcp`\n\nPlus two new columns on `repo_checkpoint_analyses` for scalar aggregates: `transcript_tokens` and `files_changed`.\n\n**Write path** — analysis-queue worker (`generateAndStoreReview`) writes facet rows + scalar columns immediately after `markComplete` succeeds. Idempotent under retries (DELETE-then-INSERT inside a transaction for the facet tables; plain UPDATE for the scalars).\n\n**Read path** — `db.analyses.aggregateFacetsByAgent` does per-agent fan-out: 4 parallel facet aggregates + 1 parallel scalar SUM per agent, all via `Promise.all`. Replaces the JS-side `mergeAnalysesInto` loop in `recap.ts`.\n\n**Backfill** — one-off cursor-paginated script (`scripts/backfill-analysis-facets.ts`) that reads existing `repo_checkpoint_analyses.analysis_json` rows, parses each blob, and upserts the derived rows. Idempotent. Supports `--dry-run` and `--limit=N`.\n\n**Feature flag** — `USE_FACET_AGGREGATOR=true` (default) routes through SQL aggregation; `=false` falls back to legacy `mergeAnalysesInto`. Kept for 24h post-deploy as a fast-rollback escape hatch (requires a redeploy to flip), removed in a follow-up.\n\n## Validation (on partial.to staging)\n\n| Range | hit1 (cold) | hit2 (warm) | hit3 (warm) |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `--day` | 2.17s | 0.91s | 0.70s |\n| `--week` | 1.02s | 1.10s | 0.85s |\n| `--month` | 1.40s | 1.26s | 0.92s |\n| `--90` | 1.42s | 1.56s | 1.91s |\n\nAll 200s. **Backfill hasn't run on partial.to yet** — the remaining 1-2s is dominated by the upstream checkpoint queries (`getByUser`, `getTeamOnUserRepos`), unchanged from #1604. The labels/skills/tool_mix aggregation cost is already minimal.\n\nPre-refactor baseline: 60s+ on local wrangler. Architecture change confirmed working end-to-end on real Cloudflare Workers + real PlanetScale data.\n\n## Rollout sequence\n\n1. Merge #1604 first (slim endpoint).\n2. Merge this PR — schema + worker writes + read path switch.\n3. Run backfill against entire.io: `pnpm --dir api exec tsx scripts/backfill-analysis-facets.ts`.\n4. 24-hour soak with `USE_FACET_AGGREGATOR=true`. If anything's off, flip the const to `false` and redeploy.\n5. Remove the flag + legacy `mergeAnalysesInto` in a follow-up PR.\n\n## Tests\n\n- Mocked-route unit tests for the SQL aggregator path in `recap.test.ts`\n- Real-MySQL integration tests for `upsertFacets`, `aggregateFacetsByCheckpointSet`, `aggregateFacetsByAgent`, and `updateScalarAggregates` in `analyses.test.ts`\n- Worker write-path tests in `analysis-queue.test.ts` covering the `markComplete`-then-write contract and the superseded-worker no-op case\n\nAll passing in CI.\n\n## Files\n\n- migration: `api/db/migrations/20260429100000_add_analysis_facet_tables.ts`\n- types: `api/src/lib/db/db-types.ts`\n- aggregator: `api/src/lib/planetscale/analyses.ts`\n- worker: `api/src/lib/analysis-queue.ts`\n- backfill: `api/scripts/backfill-analysis-facets.ts`\n- route: `api/src/routes/recap.ts`\n- tests across all of the above\n\n## Right-sizing notes\n\nThis PR went through an honest cost/value pass after the initial review feedback. We kept the structural wins that pay back at low line cost (`TOOL_MIX_CATEGORY_KEYS` shared constant, exhaustive `AnalysisFacetKind` dispatch, the small backfill bug fixes for `--limit` and narrow `catch`) and reverted the heavier review-driven additions (atomic combined-write, env-driven feature flag, parity test, full backfill test suite) because they protected against theoretical risks at meaningful line cost. The accepted tradeoffs are:\n\n1. **Rollback requires a redeploy, not an env flip.** The const-flag pattern is honest about this.\n2. **Worker-side torn-write is theoretically possible** between the facet write and the scalar UPDATE. Microsecond gap, never observed in production with the existing two-write pattern.\n3. **Backfill correctness rides on operator inspection** of resulting counts, not on automated tests of the script. It runs once.\n\nEach is fine for an internal analytics endpoint; would not be fine for a financial system. Documented here for the reviewer to weigh consciously.\nEOF\n)\" 2>&1 | tail -3","description":"Update #1737 PR body","timeout":60000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":633529,"cache_read_input_tokens":19892,"output_tokens":3630,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":633529},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":6,"output_tokens":3630,"cache_read_input_tokens":19892,"cache_creation_input_tokens":633529,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":633529,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CaZr3f775arKwmogoZa8g","type":"assistant","uuid":"e2a48419-6ca0-43fe-827c-9d86067f4662","timestamp":"2026-04-30T11:06:23.819Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/entire-activity","sessionId":"a654b6ca-4957-4d7c-8c99-62db313ff0a0","version":"2.1.119","gitBranch":"entire-activity","slug":"vectorized-whistling-bonbon"}
