{"parentUuid":"67088f00-005d-4c2b-a3f5-54706da0c467","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01UH4dwWqHjpPkE6PazLFPx6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Part 1: Agent coverage — what I found\n\n## CLI side (#1015) is agent-agnostic ✓\n\nThe CLI never filters by agent name. `MeFromMeRecap` iterates `resp.Agents` (a generic `map[string]AgentEntry`) and applies the same merge regardless of key. Tests cover `Codex` alongside `Claude Code`. Rendering in `agents_card.go` / `recap_view.go` has no Claude-specific branch. **The CLI faithfully shows whatever the API returns.**\n\n## API analysis pipeline is shaped around Claude tool names\n\nThe actual problem lives in `api/src/lib/analysis-queue.ts:extractToolMetrics`. It categorizes tools by hardcoded Claude tool names:\n\n| Tool name | Bucket |\n|---|---|\n| `Bash` | shell |\n| `Read`, `Write`, `Edit` | fileOps |\n| `Grep`, `Glob` | search |\n| `Agent`, `Skill` | agent |\n| `mcp__*` prefix | mcp |\n| anything else | other |\n\nFor non-Claude agents:\n- **Codex** emits `bash`, `apply_patch` → all land in `other`\n- **Cursor** has its own tool naming → mostly `other`\n- **OpenCode**, **FactoryAI Droid**, **Copilot CLI**, **Gemini** → similar\n- **Skills** counter only fires on Claude's `Skill` tool — so non-Claude skill arrays are always empty\n- **MCP servers** detection depends on the `mcp__*` prefix (Claude convention) — so non-Claude MCP usage isn't surfaced\n- **Labels** come from a separate LLM extraction on chunked transcript text — *those* should work for any agent\n\nThere's a unified transcript parser layer (`api/src/lib/transcript-parsers/`) with parsers for each agent that normalizes the loading side. The categorization step downstream of it didn't get the same treatment.\n\n**So what you're seeing in your recap is a real coverage gap, not a bug in #1015 or in the new endpoint.** It's been this way since the analysis pipeline shipped.\n\nThe fix lives on the API side — generalize `extractToolMetrics` to consume normalized tool taxonomies instead of raw Claude tool names. That's its own piece of work, separate from the recap endpoint.\n\n---\n\n# Part 2: Brainstorming — what I'd do differently if redoing #1015\n\nBefore I propose ideas, I want to understand which dimension you're most interested in exploring. The CLI recap codebase is ~6k lines split across ~30 files (rendering, model, view, cache, aggregation, network, TUI). A \"what would you do differently\" answer can mean very different things depending on which axis matters most to you.\n\n**Which of these matters most for the brainstorm?** (you can pick more than one)\n\n1. **Code structure** — file boundaries, package layout, what belongs where (the 6k lines feel sprawly)\n2. **Data flow** — how local-CLI data, server data, and the rendering layer hand off (currently the network-fetched data overrides local in a few places via `applyServerMe`, which is hard to reason about)\n3. **Styling / TUI architecture** — how the view-with-filters interacts with the model, how scroll/refresh/redraw work\n4. **Cross-agent handling end-to-end** — given the gap I just described, design a recap that properly supports any agent without Claude-shaped assumptions baked in\n5. **Test architecture** — there's a `testutil_test.go` at 302 lines, lots of test files; could be tighter\n6. **Something else** you've been bothered by\n\nWhich axis (or axes) do you want to dig into?"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1329,"cache_read_input_tokens":669991,"output_tokens":1659,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1329},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":1659,"cache_read_input_tokens":669991,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1329,"cache_cre