{"parentUuid":"62f2711f-42fd-4ffb-9091-ede1aebfa128","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01M7JKm29cwmJsp2iQNLGqjh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Different layers — let me unpack the data flow because the perf fix and this fix touch different parts.\n\n## What #1737's perf fix did\n\n`#1737` made the **read** fast:\n- Before: route fetched `analysis_json` blobs and aggregated in JS (60s+)\n- After: route runs `GROUP BY` against denormalized facet tables (~1s)\n\nThe data getting read is the same data — just laid out differently in storage so SQL can aggregate it without parsing JSON.\n\n## What's actually wrong for non-Claude agents\n\nThe **producer** of that data — `extractToolMetrics` — has been Claude-shaped from day 1. So when a Codex checkpoint runs through the pipeline today:\n\n```\nCodex transcript (event_msg, session_meta, ...)\n    ↓\nextractToolMetrics — looks for `type === \"assistant\"` → finds nothing\n    ↓\nanalysis_json written with: toolMix={shell:0, fileOps:0, ...}, skills=[], mcpServers=[]\n    ↓\nWorker writes facet tables from that analysis_json\n    ↓\nFacet tables for that checkpoint: empty for tool_mix/skills/mcp\n    ↓\nRecap reads facet tables → returns empty\n```\n\nSo the rows in production *today* — for every Codex/Cursor/Gemini/etc checkpoint that's already been analyzed — have **wrong (zero) data baked in** at every layer: in `analysis_json`, in the facet tables. The faster read path reads the same wrong data faster.\n\n## What \"fixing the parser\" does\n\nIf I fix `extractToolMetrics` to use each agent's parser:\n- **Going forward:** every new Codex checkpoint produces correct `analysis_json` and correct facet rows. Their recap shows real toolMix/skills/mcp.\n- **Going backward (existing rows):** nothing changes automatically. The bad zeros in `analysis_json` and facet tables stay. Recap for those old commits stays empty.\n\n## Why \"backfill\" comes up\n\nThe question is: do you want the existing thousands of Codex/Cursor/Gemini checkpoints to *retroactively* show correct toolMix/skills, or do you accept that:\n- Anything from before the fix → blank toolMix\n- Anything after the fix → real toolMix\n- Over time, as new checkpoints accumulate, the gap fades naturally\n\nThat's the choice. **Backfill = re-extract from existing transcripts to fix old rows.** No backfill = old rows stay wrong.\n\n## My recommendation: no backfill\n\nFor your specific question — looking at your *Codex commit yesterday* — the parser fix doesn't change anything for that commit retroactively unless we backfill. But:\n- Backfill of just toolMix/skills/mcp (option C — re-extract from transcripts without re-running the LLM) is a one-shot script similar to the existing `backfill-analysis-facets.ts`. Maybe ~150 lines.\n- Re-running full analysis (option B — burn tokens for re-analysis) is the wrong answer because labels are already correct; only the deterministic post-extraction is wrong.\n\nSo the real question is: do you want a one-shot script that re-extracts toolMix from existing `analysis_json` transcripts and updates the facet tables for non-Claude checkpoints? Or accept they stay empty and wait for the data to age out as new checkpoints accumulate?\n\nIf your honest answer is \"I want my recap to show correct data for the work I did yesterday on Codex\" — then yes, we need a small backfill script as part of the parser-fix PR. If your answer is \"the 24-hour soak window is fine and I don't mind old data being slightly off\" — then no backfill needed.\n\nWhich framing fits?"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2463,"cache_read_input_tokens":692545,"output_tokens":2690,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2463},"inference_geo":"","it