{"parentUuid":"1fbef8dd-adc3-453d-bf1d-faf86991c048","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01AMMhVowkSRS82SVsPM4tSU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"You're right — and that flips the answer. Since neither PR is merged, no user has seen this data yet, so \"old vs new\" is meaningless from a UX standpoint. When #1604 + #1737 land, every existing non-Claude checkpoint will be visible via `entire recap` for the first time. If toolMix/skills/mcp are wrong for those, every user's first impression of recap on their non-Claude work is \"empty bars.\"\n\n**So yes, we backfill — and the cost is small because we don't re-run the LLM.**\n\n## What \"backfill\" actually means here\n\nThe labels for existing checkpoints (LLM-extracted) are already correct for every agent — that path always went through the unified parser. The wrong data is *only* the deterministic post-processing: toolMix, skills, mcpServers. We can re-compute those from the existing transcript without burning a single Anthropic token.\n\n## Clean two-step backfill\n\nThe data moves through two layers — we fix each in order:\n\n1. **Re-extract tool metrics for existing `repo_checkpoint_analyses` rows.** New script: read each row's transcript (already stored in v1 checkpoints repo / v2 transcript-storage), re-run the (now agent-aware) `extractToolMetrics`, update only the affected fields in `analysis_json` (`toolProfile`, `skillsUsed`, `mcpServersUsed`). Leave labels, totals, scalars alone.\n\n2. **Re-run the existing facet backfill** (`scripts/backfill-analysis-facets.ts`, already part of #1737) to repopulate the facet tables from the now-corrected `analysis_json`.\n\nStep 2 already exists. Step 1 is the new piece.\n\n## Final scope for the PR\n\n1. **Parser interface change**: add `getToolCalls()`, `getSkillsUsed()`, `getMcpServersUsed()` to the parser interface\n2. **Parser implementations** for: claude-code, codex, cursor, gemini, fallback (5 agents — the ones we ship in `e2e/`)\n3. **Refactor `extractToolMetrics`** to consume parser output instead of raw JSONL\n4. **New backfill script**: `backfill-analysis-tool-metrics.ts` — re-extracts toolMix/skills/mcp from existing transcripts, updates `analysis_json` only\n5. **Tests**: per-parser unit tests against representative transcript fixtures + a refactor test for `extractToolMetrics`\n\nAfter this PR + the existing facet backfill (already in #1737):\n- Every existing checkpoint gets the right toolMix/skills/mcp regardless of agent\n- Every new checkpoint gets it correctly via the production write path\n- Users' first view of recap shows accurate data for their entire history\n\n## Rollout sequence (if all three PRs land)\n\n1. Merge `#1604` (slim endpoint)\n2. Merge `#1737` (perf via SQL aggregation)\n3. Merge **this new PR** (parser fix + tool-metrics backfill)\n4. Run **tool-metrics backfill** on production (re-extracts toolMix from existing transcripts → updates `analysis_json`)\n5. Run **facet backfill** from #1737 (writes corrected `analysis_json` data into the facet tables)\n6. Soak\n\nIf we land them out of order — the backfill on #1737 alone, then this fix later — we'd need to re-run #1737's facet backfill again after step 4 to overwrite the stale facet rows. Cleanest is to merge this PR before running either backfill.\n\n---\n\n**Does this scope work?** Specifically:\n- 5 parsers (claude / codex / cursor / gemini / fallback)\n- Two-step backfill (new tool-metrics script + existing facet script)\n- Branched off `main` on `entirehq/entire.io`\n- New PR, lands before either backfill runs\n\nConfirm and I'll draft the design doc + start."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2962,"cache_read_input_tokens":695008,"output_tokens":4086,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_toke