{"parentUuid":"93ffd433-1250-4950-b77e-fc5a9fb50b49","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01BneheWUN5omdDJNYWwYK8s","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01KySSo2oYLYciKrrs8nfZoN","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/entire-activity/docs/superpowers/plans/2026-04-30-agent-aware-tool-metrics.md","content":"# Agent-Aware Tool Metrics Implementation Plan\n\n> **For agentic workers:** REQUIRED: Use superpowers:subagent-driven-development (if subagents available) or superpowers:executing-plans to implement this plan. Steps use checkbox (`- [ ]`) syntax for tracking.\n\n**Goal:** Make `/me/recap`'s per-agent toolMix / skills / mcpServers correct for every agent (Codex, Cursor, Gemini, fallback), not just Claude Code, so users see real data on their non-Claude work the first time the recap endpoint goes live.\n\n**Architecture:** The transcript parsers already normalize each agent's native format into a shared `TranscriptMessage[]` shape that carries `toolCalls?: ToolCall[]`. The current `extractToolMetrics` ignores that and re-scans the raw JSONL with Claude-shaped assumptions (`type === \"assistant\"` + `mcp__*` prefix + `Skill` tool name), so non-Claude transcripts produce all-zero results. This plan inverts the dependency: each parser exposes an agent-specific tool classifier, and a refactored `extractToolMetrics` consumes parser output instead of raw JSONL. A small backfill script re-extracts metrics for existing `repo_checkpoint_analyses` rows (no LLM calls — labels are already correct, only the deterministic post-processing was wrong).\n\n**Tech Stack:** TypeScript, Cloudflare Workers (workerd), Kysely + PlanetScale MySQL, Vitest, oxfmt, oxlint.\n\n---\n\n## Context: where this lands\n\n- **Repo:** `entirehq/entire.io` (the API + frontend monorepo)\n- **Branch:** new branch `fix/agent-aware-tool-metrics` off `main`\n- **Worktree:** `/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/entire.io/.worktrees/agent-tool-metrics` (create fresh)\n- **Pairs with:** PRs #1604 (recap endpoint) and #1737 (perf) — those should merge first; this PR fixes the producer side that feeds them.\n- **Rollout sequence:** merge #1604 → merge #1737 → merge this PR → run **tool-metrics backfill** (this PR's new script) → run **facet backfill** (already in #1737) → soak.\n\n## File structure\n\n| File | Purpose | Status |\n|---|---|---|\n| `api/src/lib/transcript-parsers/types.ts` | Add three optional methods to `TranscriptParser` interface: `classifyTool`, `extractSkillFromTool`, `extractMcpServerFromTool` | modify |\n| `api/src/lib/transcript-parsers/tool-categories.ts` | New file: `ToolMixCategory` type + shared default classifier (returns `\"other\"`). Re-exports `TOOL_MIX_CATEGORY_KEYS` from `../../types` for cross-package use. | create |\n| `api/src/lib/transcript-parsers/claude-code-parser.ts` | Implement the three methods using Claude's tool naming (`Bash`, `Read`/`Write`/`Edit`, `Grep`/`Glob`, `mcp__*`, `Skill`/`Agent`) | modify |\n| `api/src/lib/transcript-parsers/codex-parser.ts` | Implement the three methods using Codex's tool naming (`bash`, `apply_patch`, `read_file`, etc.) | modify |\n| `api/src/lib/transcript-parsers/cursor-parser.ts` | Implement using Cursor's tool naming | modify |\n| `api/src/lib/transcript-parsers/gemini-parser.ts` | Implement using Gemini CLI's tool naming | modify |\n| `api/src/lib/transcript-parsers/fallback-parser.ts` | Use shared default classifier (`\"other\"` for everything) | modify |\n| `api/src/lib/transcript-parsers/registry.ts` | New `getToolClassifierForAgent(agent)` helper that returns the parser's classifier, defaulting to fallback's | modify |\n| `api/src/lib/analysis-queue.ts` | Refactor `extractToolMetrics` to consume parsed `TranscriptMessage[]` and dispatch via agent-specific classifier | modify |\n| `api/src/lib/analysis-queue.test.ts` | Update existing tests for new `extractToolMetrics` signature; add agent-coverage test cases (Codex, Cursor, Gemini fixtures) | modify |\n| `api/scripts/backfill-analysis-tool-metrics.ts` | New one-shot script: re-extract toolMix / skills / mcpServers for existing `repo_checkpoint_analyses` rows by reloading transcripts and re-running `extractToolMetrics`. Updates `analysis_json` only. | create |\n| `api/scripts/backfill-analysis-tool-metrics.test.ts` | Unit tests for the script's core (idempotency, agent dispatch, dry-run honoring `--limit`, narrow `catch` to `SyntaxError`) | create |\n| `api/test/planetscale/transcript-parsers/*.fixtures.json` | Real transcript fixtures captured from each agent's checkpoint output (Codex / Cursor / Gemini) for parser tests | create |\n| `api/vitest.unit.config.ts` | Add the new backfill test file to the `include` array | modify |\n\n## Tasks\n\n## Chunk 1: Shared types + Claude classifier (baseline)\n\n### Task 1: Add `ToolMixCategory` type + shared shape to transcript-parsers package\n\n**Files:**\n- Create: `api/src/lib/transcript-parsers/tool-categories.ts`\n\n- [ ] **Step 1: Write the failing test**\n\n```ts\n// api/src/lib/transcript-parsers/tool-categories.test.ts\nimport { describe, expect, it } from \"vitest\"\nimport { defaultToolClassifier, TOOL_MIX_CATEGORIES } from \"./tool-categories\"\n\ndescribe(\"tool-categories\", () => {\n  it(\"exposes the same keys as TOOL_MIX_CATEGORY_KEYS in src/types\", () => {\n    expect([...TOOL_MIX_CATEGORIES]).toEqual([\n      \"shell\",\n      \"fileOps\",\n      \"search\",\n      \"mcp\",\n      \"agent\",\n      \"other\",\n    ])\n  })\n\n  it(\"default classifier returns 'other' for any tool name\", () => {\n    expect(defaultToolClassifier({ name: \"anything\", input: {} } as never)).toBe(\"other\")\n  })\n})\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 2: Run test to verify it fails**\n\nRun: `cd api && pnpm vitest run src/lib/transcript-parsers/tool-categories.test.ts`\nExpected: FAIL with module not found.\n\n- [ ] **Ste