cript, Cloudflare Workers (workerd), Kysely + PlanetScale MySQL, Vitest, oxfmt, oxlint.\n\n---\n\n## Context: where this lands\n\n- **Repo:** `entirehq/entire.io` (the API + frontend monorepo)\n- **Branch:** new branch `fix/agent-aware-tool-metrics` off `main`\n- **Worktree:** `/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/entire.io/.worktrees/agent-tool-metrics` (create fresh)\n- **Pairs with:** PRs #1604 (recap endpoint) and #1737 (perf) — those should merge first; this PR fixes the producer side that feeds them.\n- **Rollout sequence:** merge #1604 → merge #1737 → merge this PR → run **tool-metrics backfill** (this PR's new script) → run **facet backfill** (already in #1737) → soak.\n\n## File structure\n\n| File | Purpose | Status |\n|---|---|---|\n| `api/src/lib/transcript-parsers/types.ts` | Add three optional methods to `TranscriptParser` interface: `classifyTool`, `extractSkillFromTool`, `extractMcpServerFromTool` | modify |\n| `api/src/lib/transcript-parsers/tool-categories.ts` | New file: `ToolMixCategory` type + shared default classifier (returns `\"other\"`). Re-exports `TOOL_MIX_CATEGORY_KEYS` from `../../types` for cross-package use. | create |\n| `api/src/lib/transcript-parsers/claude-code-parser.ts` | Implement the three methods using Claude's tool naming (`Bash`, `Read`/`Write`/`Edit`, `Grep`/`Glob`, `mcp__*`, `Skill`/`Agent`) | modify |\n| `api/src/lib/transcript-parsers/codex-parser.ts` | Implement the three methods using Codex's tool naming (`bash`, `apply_patch`, `read_file`, etc.) | modify |\n| `api/src/lib/transcript-parsers/cursor-parser.ts` | Implement using Cursor's tool naming | modify |\n| `api/src/lib/transcript-parsers/gemini-parser.ts` | Implement using Gemini CLI's tool naming | modify |\n| `api/src/lib/transcript-parsers/fallback-parser.ts` | Use shared default classifier (`\"other\"` for everything) | modify |\n| `api/src/lib/transcript-parsers/registry.ts` | New `getToolClassifierForAgent(agent)` helper that returns the parser's classifier, defaulting to fallback's | modify |\n| `api/src/lib/analysis-queue.ts` | Refactor `extractToolMetrics` to consume parsed `TranscriptMessage[]` and dispatch via agent-specific classifier | modify |\n| `api/src/lib/analysis-queue.test.ts` | Update existing tests for new `extractToolMetrics` signature; add agent-coverage test cases (Codex, Cursor, Gemini fixtures) | modify |\n| `api/scripts/backfill-analysis-tool-metrics.ts` | New one-shot script: re-extract toolMix / skills / mcpServers for existing `repo_checkpoint_analyses` rows by reloading transcripts and re-running `extractToolMetrics`. Updates `analysis_json` only. | create |\n| `api/scripts/backfill-analysis-tool-metrics.test.ts` | Unit tests for the script's core (idempotency, agent dispatch, dry-run honoring `--limit`, narrow `catch` to `SyntaxError`) | create |\n| `api/test/planetscale/transcript-parsers/*.fixtures.json` | Real transcript fixtures captured from each agent's checkpoint output (Codex / Cursor / Gemini) for parser tests | create |\n| `api/vitest.unit.config.ts` | Add the new backfill test file to the `include` array | modify |\n\n## Tasks\n\n## Chunk 1: Shared types + Claude classifier (baseline)\n\n### Task 1: Add `ToolMixCategory` type + shared shape to transcript-parsers package\n\n**Files:**\n- Create: `api/src/lib/transcript-parsers/tool-categories.ts`\n\n- [ ] **Step 1: Write the failing test**\n\n```ts\n// api/src/lib/transcript-parsers/tool-categories.test.ts\nimport { describe, expect, it } from \"vitest\"\nimport { defaultToolClassifier, TOOL_MIX_CATEGORIES } from \"./tool-categories\"\n\ndescribe(\"tool-categories\", () => {\n  it(\"exposes the same keys as TOOL_MIX_CATEGORY_KEYS in src/types\", () => {\n    expect([...TOOL_MIX_CATEGORIES]).toEqual([\n      \"shell\",\n      \"fileOps\",\n      \"search\",\n      \"mcp\",\n      \"agent\",\n      \"other\",\n    ])\n  })\n\n  it(\"default classifier returns 'other' for any tool name\", () => {\n    expect(defaultToolClassifier({ name: \"anything\", input: {} } as never)).toBe(\"other\")\n  })\n})\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 2: Run test to verify it fails**\n\nRun: `cd api && pnpm vitest run src/lib/transcript-parsers/tool-categories.test.ts`\nExpected: FAIL with module not found.\n\n- [ ] **Step 3: Implement minimal module**\n\n```ts\n// api/src/lib/transcript-parsers/tool-categories.ts\nimport type { ToolCall } from \"../../types\"\nimport { TOOL_MIX_CATEGORY_KEYS, type ToolMixCategoryKey } from \"../../types\"\n\n/** Re-export the canonical category list so parsers don't need to reach across packages. */\nexport const TOOL_MIX_CATEGORIES = TOOL_MIX_CATEGORY_KEYS\nexport type ToolMixCategory = ToolMixCategoryKey\n\n/** Default classifier — used by fallback parser and any parser that hasn't implemented its own yet. */\nexport function defaultToolClassifier(_call: ToolCall): ToolMixCategory {\n  return \"other\"\n}\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 4: Run test to verify it passes**\n\nRun: `cd api && pnpm vitest run src/lib/transcript-parsers/tool-categories.test.ts`\nExpected: PASS.\n\n- [ ] **Step 5: Commit**\n\n```bash\ngit add api/src/lib/transcript-parsers/tool-categories.ts api/src/lib/transcript-parsers/tool-categories.test.ts\ngit commit -m \"feat(recap-tools): add shared ToolMixCategory type + default classifier\"\n```\n\n### Task 2: Extend `TranscriptParser` interface with three optional methods\n\n**Files:**\n- Modify: `api/src/lib/transcript-parsers/types.ts`\n\n- [ ] **Step 1: Write a failing typecheck-driver test**\n\nThe test ensures the interface compiles with three new optional members. Since interfaces aren't directly testable at runtime, we exercise the contract by writing a mock parser that implements them and asserting the methods are callable.\n\n```ts\n// api/src/lib/transcript-parsers/types.test.ts\nimport { describe, expect, it } from \"vitest\"\nimport type { ToolCall } from \"../../types\"\nimport type { TranscriptParser } from \"./types\"\n\ndescribe(\"TranscriptParser optional tool-classification surface\", () => {\n  it(\"allows parsers to declare classifyTool / extractSkillFromTool / extractMcpServerFromTool\", () => {\n    const parser: TranscriptParser = {\n      name: \"test\",\n      format: \"jsonl\",\n      parse: () => ({ messages: [], isFallback: false }),\n      classifyTool: (_call: ToolCall) => \"shell\",\n      extractSkillFromTool: (_call: ToolCall) => null,\n      extractMcpServerFromTool: (_call: ToolCall) => null,\n    }\n    expect(parser.classifyTool?.({ name: \"Bash\", input: {} } as never)).toBe(\"shell\")\n  })\n})\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 2: Run test to verify it fails**\n\nRun: `cd api && pnpm vitest run src/lib/transcript-parsers/types.test.ts`\nExpected: FAIL with TS errors that `classifyTool` is not on `TranscriptParser`.\n\n- [ ] **Step 3: Extend the interface**\n\nIn `api/src/lib/transcript-parsers/types.ts`, after the existing `parseFrom?` method, add:\n\n```ts\n  /**\n   * Classify a tool call into the shared toolMix bucket. Optional — when not\n   * implemented, the registry falls back to the default classifier\n   * (returns \"other\" for everything). Each agent's tool naming is its own\n   * vocabulary; the classifier is the agent's mapping into the shared\n   * shell|fileOps|search|mcp|agent|other taxonomy.\n   */\n  classifyTool?(call: ToolCall): ToolMixCategory\n  /**\n   * Extract a skill name from a tool call, when applicable. Returns null when\n   * the call doesn't represent a skill invocation. Claude implements via the\n   * `Skill` tool; other agents return null today (no equivalent surface yet).\n   */\n  extractSkillFromTool?(call: ToolCall): string | null\n  /**\n   * Extract an MCP server name from a tool call, when applicable. Returns\n   * null when the call isn't an MCP invocation. Claude implements by parsing\n   * the `mcp__server__tool` prefix convention; other agents return null\n   * until they grow the same convention.\n   */\n  extractMcpServerFromTool?(call: ToolCall): string | null\n```\n\nAdd the imports at the top:\n\n```ts\nimport type { ToolCall } from \"../../types\"\nimport type { ToolMixCategory } from \"./tool-categories\"\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 4: Run test to verify it passes**\n\nRun: `cd api && pnpm vitest run src/lib/transcript-parsers/types.test.ts && pnpm typecheck`\nExpected: PASS.\n\n- [ ] **Step 5: Commit**\n\n```bash\ngit add api/src/lib/transcript-parsers/types.ts api/src/lib/transcript-parsers/types.test.ts\ngit commit -m \"feat(recap-tools): extend TranscriptParser with classifyTool / skill / mcp helpers\"\n```\n\n### Task 3: Implement Claude Code classifier (baseline behavior)\n\n**Files:**\n- Modify: `api/src/lib/transcript-parsers/claude-code-parser.ts`\n\n- [ ] **Step 1: Write failing tests**\n\n```ts\n// add to api/src/lib/transcript-parsers/claude-code-parser.test.ts\ndescribe(\"ClaudeCodeParser tool classification\", () => {\n  const parser = new ClaudeCodeParser()\n  const make = (name: string, input: Record<string, unknown> = {}) =>\n    ({ id: \"x\", name, input, timestamp: \"\" }) as ToolCall\n\n  it(\"classifies Bash as shell\", () => {\n    expect(parser.classifyTool!(make(\"Bash\"))).toBe(\"shell\")\n  })\n  it.each([\"Read\", \"Write\", \"Edit\"])(\"classifies %s as fileOps\", (name) => {\n    expect(parser.classifyTool!(make(name))).toBe(\"fileOps\")\n  })\n  it.each([\"Grep\", \"Glob\"])(\"classifies %s as search\", (name) => {\n    expect(parser.classifyTool!(make(name))).toBe(\"search\")\n  })\n  it.each([\"Skill\", \"Agent\"])(\"classifies %s as agent\", (name) => {\n    expect(parser.classifyTool!(make(name))).toBe(\"agent\")\n  })\n  it(\"classifies mcp__github__list_issues as mcp\", () => {\n    expect(parser.classifyTool!(make(\"mcp__github__list_issues\"))).toBe(\"mcp\")\n  })\n  it(\"classifies unknown tools as other\", () => {\n    expect(parser.classifyTool!(make(\"WebFetch\"))).toBe(\"other\")\n  })\n\n  it(\"extracts skill name from Skill tool input\", () => {\n    expect(parser.extractSkillFromTool!(make(\"Skill\", { skill: \"debugging\" }))).toBe(\"debugging\")\n  })\n  it(\"returns null for non-Skill tool calls\", () => {\n    expect(parser.extractSkillFromTool!(make(\"Bash\"))).toBeNull()\n  })\n  it(\"returns null when Skill tool input lacks skill name\", () => {\n    expect(parser.extractSkillFromTool!(make(\"Skill\", {}))).toBeNull()\n  })\n\n  it(\"extracts mcp server from mcp__github__list_issues\", () => {\n    expect(parser.extractMcpServerFromTool!(make(\"mcp__github__list_issues\"))).toBe(\"github\")\n  })\n  it(\"returns null for non-MCP calls\", () => {\n    expect(parser.extractMcpServerFromTool!(make(\"Bash\"))).toBeNull()\n  })\n})\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 2: Run tests to verify they fail**\n\nRun: `cd api && pnpm vitest run src/lib/transcript-parsers/claude-code-parser.test.ts`\nExpected: FAIL — methods not implemented.\n\n- [ ] **Step 3: Implement on `ClaudeCodeParser`**\n\nAdd three methods to the class in `claude-code-parser.ts`:\n\n```ts\nclassifyTool(call: ToolCall): ToolMixCategory {\n  const name = call.name\n  if (name === \"Bash\") return \"shell\"\n  if (name === \"Read\" || name === \"Write\" || name === \"Edit\") return \"fileOps\"\n  if (name === \"Grep\" || name === \"Glob\") return \"search\"\n  if (name === \"Skill\" || name === \"Agent\") return \"agent\"\n  if (name.startsWith(\"mcp__\")) return \"mcp\"\n  return \"other\"\n}\n\nextractSkillFromTool(call: ToolCall): string | null {\n  if (call.name !== \"Skill\") return null\n  const skill = (call.input as Record<string, unknown>)?.skill\n  return typeof skill === \"string\" && skill.length > 0 ? skill : null\n}\n\nextractMcpServerFromTool(call: ToolCall): string | null {\n  if (!call.name.startsWith(\"mcp__\")) return null\n  const segments = call.name.split(\"__\")\n  return segments.length >= 3 && segments[1] ? segments[1] : null\n}\n```\n\nAdd imports:\n\n```ts\nimport type { ToolMixCategory } from \"./tool-categories\"\n```\n\n`ToolCall` is already imported.\n\n