st on `main` yet** — it's only on the `feat/recap-facets-sql-agg` branch (#1737). My plan branches off `main`, so there's no model to copy.\n- Idempotency, cursor advancement, sessions-empty check, and JSON merge semantics are all under-specified.\n- Task 12 (tests) is ordered after Task 11 (implementation) — inverts TDD.\n\n### Chunk 5 — Issues Found ⚠️\n- Pre-push gauntlet uses `test:unit` (curated subset); CI runs full `test:run` against MySQL workers. A test that breaks under the full config but passes under unit would land green locally / red in CI.\n- Missing DB-types drift check (CI runs it).\n- PR body says \"pinned numbers\" but Task 10's actual assertion is `total > 0`.\n\n---\n\n## My read on next steps\n\nTwo of the issues (Codex tool names, missing model script on `main`) make me question whether the plan's framing is right at all. Specifically:\n\n1. **The Codex classifier needs ~6-7 specific tool names mapped, not the 2-3 I sketched.** That's a research task, not a \"implementer fills it in.\" Worth doing right in the plan since it's load-bearing.\n\n2. **Stacking vs forking.** If we branch off `main`, the backfill script is standalone (no model to mirror). If we stack on `feat/recap-facets-sql-agg` (#1737), we re-use that branch's structure but create another stacked PR. The plan assumed a model existed on `main` — neither option matches that.\n\n3. **Cursor's classifier is currently dead code.** Either the plan adds a Cursor-parser change to surface toolCalls (scope creep), or it explicitly defers Cursor with a comment.\n\nI think the right move is **revise the plan with the critical fixes baked in**, then re-run the reviewer on revised chunks. The minor issues (TDD framing nits, advisory recommendations) can ride along.\n\nThree options for how to proceed:\n\n- **A. Full plan revision.** I rewrite the affected sections (~most of Chunks 2 and 4) and re-run the chunk-by-chunk reviewer. ~30 min before any code is touched.\n- **B. Trim the plan and execute looser.** Acknowledge the plan as a sketch; execute task by task with you in the loop on each chunk's specific decisions (tool name list, branching choice, etc.). Less upfront cost, more interactive.\n- **C. Drop Chunk 4 (backfill) from this PR entirely.** Ship just Chunks 1-3 (parser fix → producer correctness for new checkpoints). Backfill becomes a follow-up that benefits from the perf branch's actual `runBackfill` model once it merges. Smaller surface, faster shipping.\n\nHonest preference: **C**, then **B**. The backfill is what makes \"no users have seen this yet → all data is new\" meaningful. But it's the part where the plan went sideways. If we ship just the producer fix first, every NEW checkpoint after merge is correct, and the backfill becomes a focused follow-up against an actual model script.\n\nWhich direction?"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8875,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3872,"cache_read_input_tokens":738064,"output_tokens":5280,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3872},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":8875,"output_tokens":5280,"cache_read_input_tokens":738064,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3872,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3872,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CaZv7X3kFThMVQENV6N3Z","type":"assistant","uuid":"29409bee-f623-48f7-a8b4-73962734833a","timestamp":"2026-04-30T12:00:17.144Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/entire-activity","sessionId":"a654b6ca-4957-4d7c-8c99-62db313ff0a0","version":"2.1.119","gitBranch":"entire-activity","slug":"vectorized-whistling-bonbon"}
