fier (mirror Task 5)","new_string":"## Chunk 2: Codex / Gemini / fallback classifiers\n\n### Task 4: Capture Codex tool-name fixture from a real transcript\n\n**Files:**\n- Create: `api/test/transcript-parsers/codex-tool-names.fixtures.json`\n\nThe Codex transcript at the cli repo's `entire/checkpoints/v1:7a/9387cf9003/0/full.jsonl` (from commit `a9e6e67b6e74ef97a632799691bb0266be19fdf9`) is the canonical fixture source. We capture the actual tool-name distribution so Task 5's classifier covers names that occur in real production data, not invented examples.\n\nThe expected output of the script below — based on a real run we did during planning — is:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"exec_command\": 221,\n  \"write_stdin\": 55,\n  \"apply_patch\": 11,\n  \"update_plan\": 4,\n  \"_list_pull_request_review_threads\": 4,\n  \"_fetch_pr_comments\": 2\n}\n```\n\nThese are the load-bearing names the Task 5 classifier MUST handle. If the script below produces a meaningfully different distribution (e.g., a fresh transcript with different tools), the classifier in Task 5 needs to be extended to cover whatever the script returned — the principle is \"no zeros for real Codex data.\"\n\n- [ ] **Step 1: Extract observed tool names from the cli repo's checkpoint store**\n\nRun from the worktree root (note: this is the **cli** repo, where the checkpoint metadata lives, not the entire.io API repo where the fix is):\n\n```bash\ncd /Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/entire-activity\ngit show entire/checkpoints/v1:7a/9387cf9003/0/full.jsonl | \\\n  python3 -c \"\nimport sys, json, collections\ncounts = collections.Counter()\nfor line in sys.stdin:\n    line = line.strip()\n    if not line: continue\n    try: o = json.loads(line)\n    except: continue\n    p = o.get('payload', {})\n    t = p.get('type') if isinstance(p, dict) else None\n    if t in ('function_call', 'custom_tool_call', 'local_shell_call'):\n        nm = p.get('name')\n        if not nm and isinstance(p.get('tool_call'), dict):\n            nm = p['tool_call'].get('name')\n        if nm: counts[nm] += 1\nprint(json.dumps(dict(counts.most_common()), indent=2))\n\" > /tmp/codex-tool-names.json\ncat /tmp/codex-tool-names.json\n```\n\nExpected output: the JSON shown above (or a similar distribution from a different transcript).\n\n- [ ] **Step 2: Move the fixture into the API worktree and stage it**\n\nThe fixture lives in the **entire.io** repo where the test consumes it. Create the directory in that worktree, copy the captured JSON, then `git add` from there:\n\n```bash\ncd /Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/entire.io/.worktrees/agent-tool-metrics\nmkdir -p api/test/transcript-parsers\ncp /tmp/codex-tool-names.json api/test/transcript-parsers/codex-tool-names.fixtures.json\ngit add api/test/transcript-parsers/codex-tool-names.fixtures.json\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 3: Commit**\n\n```bash\ngit commit -m \"test(recap-tools): capture Codex tool-name fixture from real transcript\"\n```\n\n### Task 5: Implement Codex classifier with real-name coverage\n\n**Files:**\n- Modify: `api/src/lib/transcript-parsers/codex-parser.ts`\n- Modify: `api/src/lib/transcript-parsers/codex-parser.test.ts`\n\nThe classifier maps Codex's actual tool vocabulary into the shared 6-bucket taxonomy. Mappings derived from the captured fixture and Codex's transcript schema:\n\n| Codex tool name | Bucket | Reasoning |\n|---|---|---|\n| `exec_command` | shell | Codex's primary shell-execution path (most common in fixture) |\n| `local_shell_call` | shell | Codex's synthetic name for `local_shell_call` payload type (the parser already maps this in `parse()`) |\n| `write_stdin` | shell | Writes to a running shell process — clearly shell category |\n| `bash`, `shell` | shell | Defensive aliases for transcripts that use these names directly |\n| `apply_patch` | fileOps | Codex's patch-application tool |\n| `read_file`, `write_file`, `edit` | fileOps | Common file-op names if transcripts use them |\n| `update_plan` | agent | Plan/track-list management — agent-orchestration category |\n| Names starting with `_` (underscore prefix) | mcp | Codex MCP-tool naming convention (e.g., `_list_pull_request_review_threads`, `_fetch_pr_comments`) |\n| anything else | other | Explicit \"we don't know yet\" bucket |\n\n- [ ] **Step 1: Write failing tests pinning each real-fixture name to its bucket**\n\n```ts\n// add to api/src/lib/transcript-parsers/codex-parser.test.ts\nimport fixture from \"../../../test/transcript-parsers/codex-tool-names.fixtures.json\"\n\ndescribe(\"CodexParser tool classification\", () => {\n  const parser = new CodexParser()\n  const make = (name: string, input: Record<string, unknown> = {}) =>\n    ({ id: \"x\", name, input, timestamp: \"\" }) as ToolCall\n\n  // Pin specific names from the captured fixture to specific buckets — not\n  // a regex match. Vague-passing tests are how the original Claude-shaped\n  // bug shipped; this prevents the classifier from regressing into \"everything\n  // is 'other'.\"\n  it(\"classifies exec_command (Codex's primary shell tool) as shell\", () => {\n    expect(parser.classifyTool!(make(\"exec_command\"))).toBe(\"shell\")\n  })\n  it(\"classifies write_stdin as shell\", () => {\n    expect(parser.classifyTool!(make(\"write_stdin\"))).toBe(\"shell\")\n  })\n  it(\"classifies local_shell_call as shell (Codex synthetic name)\", () => {\n    expect(parser.classifyTool!(make(\"local_shell_call\"))).toBe(\"shell\")\n  })\n  it(\"classifies apply_patch as fileOps\", () => {\n    expect(parser.classifyTool!(make(\"apply_patch\"))).toBe(\"fileOps\")\n  })\n  it(\"classifies update_plan as agent\", () => {\n    expect(parser.classifyTool!(make(\"update_plan\"))).toBe(\"agent\")\n  })\n  it(\"classifies underscore-prefixed names as mcp (Codex MCP convention)\", () => {\n    expect(parser.classifyTool!(make(\"_list_pull_request_review_threads\"))).toBe(\"mcp\")\n    expect(parser.classifyTool!(make(\"_fetch_pr_comments\"))).toBe(\"mcp\")\n  })\n  it(\"returns 'other' for unrecognized Codex tools\", () => {\n    expect(parser.classifyTool!(make(\"definitely_not_a_codex_tool\"))).toBe(\"other\")\n  })\n  it(\"every fixture tool name lands in a non-other bucket\", () => {\n    // The captured fixture is real production Codex data. If any name there\n    // ends up in 'other', it's a coverage hole — fix the classifier.\n    const dropped: string[] = []\n    for (const name of Object.keys(fixture)) {\n      if (parser.classifyTool!(make(name)) === \"other\") dropped.push(name)\n    }\n    expect(dropped).toEqual([])\n  })\n  it(\"returns null for Codex skill / mcp-server extraction (parser doesn't surface them today)\", () => {\n    expect(parser.extractSkillFromTool!(make(\"exec_command\"))).toBeNull()\n    expect(parser.extractMcpServerFromTool!(make(\"exec_command\"))).toBeNull()\n  })\n})\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 2: Run tests to verify they fail**\n\nRun: `cd api && pnpm vitest run src/lib/transcript-parsers/codex-parser.test.ts`\nExpected: FAIL — methods not implemented.\n\n- [ ] **Step 3: Implement classifier on `CodexParser` class**\n\n```ts\nclassifyTool(call: ToolCall): ToolMixCategory {\n  const name = call.name\n  if (\n    name === \"exec_command\" ||\n    name === \"local_shell_call\" ||\n    name === \"write_stdin\" ||\n    name === \"bash\" ||\n    name === \"shell\"\n  ) {\n    return \"shell\"\n  }\n  if (\n    name === \"apply_patch\" ||\n    name === \"read_file\" ||\n    name === \"write_file\" ||\n    name === \"edit\"\n  ) {\n    return \"fileOps\"\n  }\n  if (name === \"update_plan\") return \"agent\"\n  // Codex MCP-tool naming convention: leading underscore (e.g.\n  // `_list_pull_request_review_threads`, `_fetch_pr_comments`). The parser\n  // doesn't currently extract a server name from these — `extractMcpServerFromTool`\n  // returns null below — but the bucket is correct.\n  if (name.startsWith(\"_\")) return \"mcp\"\n  if (name === \"grep\" || name === \"glob\" || name === \"search\") return \"search\"\n  return \"other\"\n}\n\nextractSkillFromTool(_call: ToolCall): string | null {\n  // Codex has no equivalent of Claude's `Skill` tool today.\n  return null\n}\n\nextractMcpServerFromTool(_call: ToolCall): string | null {\n  // Codex transcripts contain `mcp_tool_call_end` payloads, but the\n  // current parser doesn't surface a server name in `toolCalls[]`.\n  // Returning null preserves recap correctness; surfacing server names\n  // is a follow-up parser change.\n  return null\n}\n```\n\nAdd the import:\n\n```ts\nimport type { ToolMixCategory } from \"./tool-categories\"\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 4: Run tests to verify they pass**\n\nRun: `cd api && pnpm vitest run src/lib/transcript-parsers/codex-parser.test.ts`\nExpected: PASS, including the \"every fixture tool name lands in a non-other bucket\" assertion.\n\n- [ ] **Step 5: Commit**\n\n```bash\ngit add api/src/lib/transcript-parsers/codex-parser.ts api/src/lib/transcript-parsers/codex-parser.test.ts\ngit commit -m \"feat(recap-tools): CodexParser exposes tool classifier with real-fixture coverage\"\n```\n\n### Task 6: Implement Gemini classifier (mirror Task 5)"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3226,"cache_read_input_tokens":766413,"output_tokens":7080,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3226,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":7080,"cache_read_input_tokens":766413,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3226,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3226},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CaZxdYcpxHwD1aATjgTKJ","type":"assistant","uuid":"4ce7ce8a-f194-4181-9aef-b9783af37ef4","timestamp":"2026-04-30T12:32:54.335Z","use