{"parentUuid":"1bf55ecb-f9c9-4b78-ab37-05a6f6baea9f","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01VUj7iFq5Sms7hKxDvLeRg1","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_017rZCuUXjavV8sV8Cw8sZvq","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/entire-activity/docs/superpowers/plans/2026-04-30-agent-aware-tool-metrics.md","old_string":"## Chunk 4: Backfill script for existing analyses\n\n### Task 10: Tests for backfill (TDD-first)\n\n**Files:**\n- Create: `api/scripts/backfill-analysis-tool-metrics.ts`\n\nMirrors `backfill-analysis-facets.ts` in shape (cursor-paginated, idempotent, `--dry-run`, `--limit=N`, narrow JSON-parse catch). The difference: this one does NOT touch the facet tables. It walks `repo_checkpoint_analyses` rows, reloads the transcript via `loadCheckpointTranscript`, runs `extractToolMetricsFromSessions`, and updates the affected fields in `analysis_json` only.\n\n- [ ] **Step 1: Create the script skeleton**\n\n```ts\n#!/usr/bin/env tsx\n/**\n * Backfill repo_checkpoint_analyses.analysis_json with corrected toolMix /\n * skills / mcpServers for non-Claude checkpoints. Idempotent — safe to\n * re-run after partial completion.\n *\n * Why: extractToolMetrics was Claude-shaped before fix/agent-aware-tool-metrics.\n * Existing rows have toolProfile=zeros and empty skills/mcp for every agent\n * other than Claude. This script re-runs the (now agent-aware) extractor\n * against existing transcripts and overwrites the three fields.\n *\n * Does NOT call the LLM — labels and other LLM-derived fields are already\n * correct for every agent because the labels path always went through the\n * unified parser.\n *\n * Usage: pnpm exec tsx scripts/backfill-analysis-tool-metrics.ts [--limit=N] [--dry-run]\n */\n\nimport { Kysely, MysqlDialect } from \"kysely\"\nimport { createPool } from \"mysql2\"\nimport type { DB } from \"../db/types\"\nimport { extractToolMetricsFromSessions, type ParsedSessionForMetrics } from \"../src/lib/analysis-queue\"\nimport { loadCheckpointTranscript } from \"../src/lib/checkpoint-transcript\"\n\n// (DB-connection helper identical to backfill-analysis-facets.ts:createDb)\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 2: Implement the loop body**\n\nThe loop is structurally identical to `backfill-analysis-facets.ts`'s `runBackfill` but with these differences:\n\n- Read both `analysis_json` and the checkpoint key (`repo_id`, `checkpoint_id`)\n- Load the transcript via `loadCheckpointTranscript(db, repoId, checkpointId, ...)`\n- Run `extractToolMetricsFromSessions(loaded.sessions.map(...))`\n- Merge the three fields into the existing parsed `analysis_json`\n- Write the updated JSON back via `UPDATE repo_checkpoint_analyses SET analysis_json = ? WHERE ...`\n\n```ts\nexport async function runBackfill(\n  deps: { db: Kysely<DB> },\n  options: { max: number; dryRun: boolean },\n): Promise<{ processed: number; skipped: number; updated: number }> {\n  // … cursor-paginated SELECT (mirror backfill-analysis-facets.ts) …\n  // For each row:\n  //   1. Parse analysis_json (narrow catch to SyntaxError)\n  //   2. Load transcript via loadCheckpointTranscript\n  //   3. If sessions empty → skip\n  //   4. Run extractToolMetricsFromSessions\n  //   5. Merge into the parsed analysis JSON\n  //   6. If dryRun → log diff, don't write\n  //   7. Else → UPDATE analysis_json\n  // Return counters\n}\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 3: Add `main()` + `if (process.argv[1] && /backfill-analysis-tool-metrics\\.ts$/.test(process.argv[1]))` guard**\n\nMirror the entry-point pattern from the facet backfill so it auto-runs as a script but stays importable for tests.\n\n- [ ] **Step 4: Format check**\n\nRun: `cd /Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/entire.io/.worktrees/agent-tool-metrics && pnpm format api/scripts/backfill-analysis-tool-metrics.ts`\n\n- [ ] **Step 5: Commit**\n\n```bash\ngit add api/scripts/backfill-analysis-tool-metrics.ts\ngit commit -m \"feat(recap-tools): backfill script re-extracts tool metrics from existing transcripts\"\n```\n\n### Task 12: Tests for backfill script\n\n**Files:**\n- Create: `api/scripts/backfill-analysis-tool-metrics.test.ts`\n- Modify: `api/vitest.unit.config.ts` (add the new test path)\n\n- [ ] **Step 1: Write tests covering happy path + dry-run + idempotency + narrow catch**\n\nMirror `backfill-analysis-facets.test.ts`. Use a fake Kysely DB and a stub `loadCheckpointTranscript`. Specifically:\n\n```ts\ndescribe(\"runBackfill (tool metrics)\", () => {\n  it(\"processes each row, updates analysis_json with corrected metrics\", async () => { /* … */ })\n  it(\"dry-run never writes — counts wouldUpdate\", async () => { /* … */ })\n  it(\"honours --limit under both real and dry-run modes\", async () => { /* … */ })\n  it(\"skips rows with malformed JSON (SyntaxError) — propagates other errors\", async () => { /* … */ })\n  it(\"skips rows where the transcript can't be loaded (no sessions)\", async () => { /* … */ })\n})\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 2: Run tests to verify they fail**\n\nRun: `cd api && pnpm vitest run scripts/backfill-analysis-tool-metrics.test.ts`\nExpected: FAIL — test file's imports of `runBackfill` should resolve, but the assertions fail until the script implementation matches.\n\n- [ ] **Step 3: Add the script's path to `vitest.unit.config.ts`**\n\nIn `api/vitest.unit.config.ts`, add `\"scripts/backfill-analysis-tool-metrics.test.ts\"` next to the existing `\"scripts/backfill-analysis-facets.test.ts\"`.\n\n- [ ] **Step 4: Run tests to verify they pass**\n\nRun: `cd api && pnpm vitest run scripts/backfill-analysis-tool-metrics.test.ts && pnpm test:unit`\nExpected: PASS, including in the curated unit suite.\n\n- [ ] **Step 5: Commit**\n\n```bash\ngit add api/scripts/backfill-analysis-tool-metrics.test.ts api/vitest.unit.config.ts\ngit commit -m \"test(recap-tools): unit tests for tool-metrics backfill (happy path, dry-run, idempotency, error narrowing)\"\n```","new_string":"## Chunk 4: Backfill script for existing analyses\n\nThe branch is off `main` so `backfill-analysis-facets.ts` (introduced in #1737) is **not present**. There's no model script to mirror. We write a standalone, tested backfill from scratch.\n\nThe script reads existing `repo_checkpoint_analyses` rows, reloads each transcript through the actual `loadCheckpointTranscript` cascade, re-runs `extractToolMetricsFromSessions`, and overwrites three fields in `analysis_json`: `toolProfile`, `skillsUsed`, `mcpServersUsed`. It does **not** touch facet tables (those don't exist on `main` yet — #1737's facet-backfill handles writing facets). It does **not** call any LLM — labels and other LLM-derived fields are already correct.\n\n**Real `loadCheckpointTranscript` signature** — from `api/src/lib/checkpoint-transcript.ts:323-348`:\n\n```ts\ninterface LoadCheckpointTranscriptArgs {\n  db: Db\n  repoId: string\n  checkpointId: string\n  checkpoint: CheckpointWithCommit\n  checkpointRepoFullName: string\n  token: string | undefined\n}\nexport async function loadCheckpointTranscript(\n  args: LoadCheckpointTranscriptArgs,\n): Promise<LoadedCheckpointTranscript>\n```\n\n`checkpoint` and `checkpointRepoFullName` are NOT on the analysis row — they require lookups. The pattern in `analysis-queue.ts:283-298` (existing code) does these lookups; the script mirrors that. `token` for the GitHub-fallback path: pass `undefined` (DB-only path is sufficient — if the transcript isn't in the DB, that's an environment-corruption case; skip the row, log it).\n\n### Task 10: Write failing tests for `runBackfill` (tests-first)\n\n**Files:**\n- Create: `api/scripts/backfill-analysis-tool-metrics.test.ts`\n\nThe script is testable via dependency injection: `runBackfill` takes a `deps` object containing the DB and a `loadTranscript` callable. Tests inject fakes for both. The CLI `main()` builds real `deps` and calls `runBackfill`.\n\n- [ ] **Step 1: Write the test