{"parentUuid":"a1069ede-b6d7-45aa-8cd6-eb8307ac37ba","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"4fe315ba-ec73-4603-98f9-7a7da8450830","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017rZCuUXjavV8sV8Cw8sZvq","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/entire-activity/docs/superpowers/plans/2026-04-30-agent-aware-tool-metrics.md has been updated successfully."}]},"uuid":"c5437e52-0008-4f35-9293-c2583e381480","timestamp":"2026-04-30T12:38:34.282Z","toolUseResult":{"filePath":"/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/entire-activity/docs/superpowers/plans/2026-04-30-agent-aware-tool-metrics.md","oldString":"## Chunk 4: Backfill script for existing analyses\n\n### Task 10: Tests for backfill (TDD-first)\n\n**Files:**\n- Create: `api/scripts/backfill-analysis-tool-metrics.ts`\n\nMirrors `backfill-analysis-facets.ts` in shape (cursor-paginated, idempotent, `--dry-run`, `--limit=N`, narrow JSON-parse catch). The difference: this one does NOT touch the facet tables. It walks `repo_checkpoint_analyses` rows, reloads the transcript via `loadCheckpointTranscript`, runs `extractToolMetricsFromSessions`, and updates the affected fields in `analysis_json` only.\n\n- [ ] **Step 1: Create the script skeleton**\n\n```ts\n#!/usr/bin/env tsx\n/**\n * Backfill repo_checkpoint_analyses.analysis_json with corrected toolMix /\n * skills / mcpServers for non-Claude checkpoints. Idempotent — safe to\n * re-run after partial completion.\n *\n * Why: extractToolMetrics was Claude-shaped before fix/agent-aware-tool-metrics.\n * Existing rows have toolProfile=zeros and empty skills/mcp for every agent\n * other than Claude. This script re-runs the (now agent-aware) extractor\n * against existing transcripts and overwrites the three fields.\n *\n * Does NOT call the LLM — labels and other LLM-derived fields are already\n * correct for every agent because the labels path always went through the\n * unified parser.\n *\n * Usage: pnpm exec tsx scripts/backfill-analysis-tool-metrics.ts [--limit=N] [--dry-run]\n */\n\nimport { Kysely, MysqlDialect } from \"kysely\"\nimport { createPool } from \"mysql2\"\nimport type { DB } from \"../db/types\"\nimport { extractToolMetricsFromSessions, type ParsedSessionForMetrics } from \"../src/lib/analysis-queue\"\nimport { loadCheckpointTranscript } from \"../src/lib/checkpoint-transcript\"\n\n// (DB-connection helper identical to backfill-analysis-facets.ts:createDb)\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 2: Implement the loop body**\n\nThe loop is structurally identical to `backfill-analysis-facets.ts`'s `runBackfill` but with these differences:\n\n- Read both `analysis_json` and the checkpoint key (`repo_id`, `checkpoint_id`)\n- Load the transcript via `loadCheckpointTranscript(db, repoId, checkpointId, ...)`\n- Run `extractToolMetricsFromSessions(loaded.sessions.map(...))`\n- Merge the three fields into the existing parsed `analysis_json`\n- Write the updated JSON back via `UPDATE repo_checkpoint_analyses SET analysis_json = ? WHERE ...`\n\n```ts\nexport async function runBackfill(\n  deps: { db: Kysely<DB> },\n  options: { max: number; dryRun: boolean },\n): Promise<{ processed: number; skipped: number; updated: number }> {\n  // … cursor-paginated SELECT (mirror backfill-analysis-facets.ts) …\n  // For each row:\n  //   1. Parse analysis_json (narrow catch to SyntaxError)\n  //   2. Load transcript via loadCheckpointTranscript\n  //   3. If sessions empty → skip\n  //   4. Run extractToolMetricsFromSessions\n  //   5. Merge into the parsed analysis JSON\n  //   6. If dryRun → log diff, don't write\n  //   7. Else → UPDATE analysis_json\n  // Return counters\n}\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 3: Add `main()` + `if (process.argv[1] && /backfill-analysis-tool-metrics\\.ts$/.test(process.argv[1]))` guard**\n\nMirror the entry-point pattern from the facet backfill so it auto-runs as a script but stays importable for tests.\n\n- [ ] **Step 4: Format