curated unit suite.\n\n- [ ] **Step 5: Commit**\n\n```bash\ngit add api/scripts/backfill-analysis-tool-metrics.test.ts api/vitest.unit.config.ts\ngit commit -m \"test(recap-tools): unit tests for tool-metrics backfill (happy path, dry-run, idempotency, error narrowing)\"\n```","newString":"## Chunk 4: Backfill script for existing analyses\n\nThe branch is off `main` so `backfill-analysis-facets.ts` (introduced in #1737) is **not present**. There's no model script to mirror. We write a standalone, tested backfill from scratch.\n\nThe script reads existing `repo_checkpoint_analyses` rows, reloads each transcript through the actual `loadCheckpointTranscript` cascade, re-runs `extractToolMetricsFromSessions`, and overwrites three fields in `analysis_json`: `toolProfile`, `skillsUsed`, `mcpServersUsed`. It does **not** touch facet tables (those don't exist on `main` yet — #1737's facet-backfill handles writing facets). It does **not** call any LLM — labels and other LLM-derived fields are already correct.\n\n**Real `loadCheckpointTranscript` signature** — from `api/src/lib/checkpoint-transcript.ts:323-348`:\n\n```ts\ninterface LoadCheckpointTranscriptArgs {\n  db: Db\n  repoId: string\n  checkpointId: string\n  checkpoint: CheckpointWithCommit\n  checkpointRepoFullName: string\n  token: string | undefined\n}\nexport async function loadCheckpointTranscript(\n  args: LoadCheckpointTranscriptArgs,\n): Promise<LoadedCheckpointTranscript>\n```\n\n`checkpoint` and `checkpointRepoFullName` are NOT on the analysis row — they require lookups. The pattern in `analysis-queue.ts:283-298` (existing code) does these lookups; the script mirrors that. `token` for the GitHub-fallback path: pass `undefined` (DB-only path is sufficient — if the transcript isn't in the DB, that's an environment-corruption case; skip the row, log it).\n\n### Task 10: Write failing tests for `runBackfill` (tests-first)\n\n**Files:**\n- Create: `api/scripts/backfill-analysis-tool-metrics.test.ts`\n\nThe script is testable via dependency injection: `runBackfill` takes a `deps` object containing the DB and a `loadTranscript` callable. Tests inject fakes for both. The CLI `main()` builds real `deps` and calls `runBackfill`.\n\n- [ ] **Step 1: Write the test file**\n\n```ts\n// api/scripts/backfill-analysis-tool-metrics.test.ts\nimport type { Kysely } from \"kysely\"\nimport { describe, expect, it, vi } from \"vitest\"\nimport type { DB } from \"../db/types\"\nimport type { SessionTranscript } from \"../src/types\"\nimport { runBackfill, type BackfillDeps } from \"./backfill-analysis-tool-metrics\"\n\n// Fake Kysely chain whose .execute() returns the queued batches in order, then\n// an empty array forever. The script only uses selectFrom/select/where/\n// orderBy/limit/execute for paging, plus updateTable/set/where/execute for\n// writes — anything else is a test-setup smell.\nfunction makeMockDb(\n  selectBatches: Array<\n    Array<{ repo_id: string; checkpoint_id: string; analysis_json: string | null }>\n  >,\n) {\n  const selectExec = vi.fn()\n  for (const b of selectBatches) selectExec.mockResolvedValueOnce(b)\n  selectExec.mockResolvedValue([])\n\n  const updateExec = vi.fn().mockResolvedValue({ numUpdatedRows: 1n })\n\n  const selectChain = {\n    selectFrom: vi.fn().mockReturnThis(),\n    select: vi.fn().mockReturnThis(),\n    where: vi.fn().mockReturnThis(),\n    orderBy: vi.fn().mockReturnThis(),\n    limit: vi.fn().mockReturnThis(),\n    execute: selectExec,\n  }\n  const updateChain = {\n    updateTable: vi.fn().mockReturnThis(),\n    set: vi.fn().mockReturnThis(),\n    where: vi.fn().mockReturnThis(),\n    execute: updateExec,\n  }\n  const db = {\n    selectFrom: selectChain.selectFrom,\n    updateTable: updateChain.updateTable,\n    // wire each chain method back to its chain so the same call walks correctly\n    ...selectChain,\n    ...updateChain,\n  } as unknown as Kysely<DB>\n  return { db, selectExec, updateExec, updateChain }\n}\n\nconst fixedAnalysisJson = JSON.stringify({\n  // Pre-existing fields the backfill must NOT touch\n  extraction: { labels: [\"bug_fix\"] },\n  total_transcript_tokens: 1234,\n  totalFilesChanged: 7,\n  // Stale Claude-shaped tool metrics that the backfill should overwrite\n  toolProfile: {\n    categories: {\n      shell: { count: 0 },\n      fileOps: { count: 0 },\n      search: { count: 0 },\n      mcp: { count: 0 },\n      agent: { count: 0 },\n      other: { count: 0 },\n    },\n    total: 0,\n  },\n  skillsUsed: [],\n  mcpServersUsed: [],\n})\n\nfunction fakeSession(agent: string, toolNames: string[]): SessionTranscript {\n  return {\n    sessionId: \"sess-1\",\n    agent,\n    messages: [\n      {\n        id: \"msg-1\",\n        role: \"assistant\",\n        content: \"\",\n        timestamp: \"2026-04-30T00:00:00Z\",\n        toolCalls: toolNames.map((name, i) => ({\n          id: `t${i}`,\n          name,\n          input: {},\n          timestamp: \"2026-04-30T00:00:00Z\",\n        })),\n      },\n    ],\n    transcriptIdentifierAtStart: null,\n    checkpointTranscriptStart: null,\n  }\n}\n\ndescribe(\"runBackfill (tool metrics)\", () => {\n  it(\"rewrites analysis_json with corrected toolProfile/skills/mcp without dropping unrelated fields\", async () => {\n    const { db, updateExec, updateChain } = makeMockDb([\n      [{ repo_id: \"r1\", checkpoint_id: \"c1\", analysis_json: fixedAnalysisJson }],\n    ])\n    const loadTranscript = vi.fn(async () => ({\n      sessions: [fakeSession(\"Codex\", [\"exec_command\", \"apply_patch\"])],\n    }))\n\n    const result = await runBackfill(\n      { db, loadTranscript } as BackfillDeps,\n      { max: Infinity, dryRun: false },\n    )\n\n    expect(result).toEqual({ processed: 1, skipped: 0, updated: 1 })\n    expect(updateExec).toHaveBeenCalledTimes(1)\n    expect(loadTranscript).toHaveBeenCalledWith({ repoId: \"r1\", checkpointId: \"c1\" })\n\n    // The .set() call's first argument is the patch object Kysely will apply.\n    const set