{"parentUuid":"7b996e2a-0d9e-4514-96a9-3c6b82683ea7","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_018RxKXLY2rWUnHF7RBk9yyc","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_019ac98F9qmVd85p1YU9TzZ4","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/entire-activity/docs/superpowers/plans/2026-04-30-agent-aware-tool-metrics.md","content":"# Agent-Aware Tool Metrics Implementation Plan\n\n> **For agentic workers:** REQUIRED: Use superpowers:subagent-driven-development (if subagents available) or superpowers:executing-plans to implement this plan. Steps use checkbox (`- [ ]`) syntax for tracking.\n\n**Goal:** Make `/me/recap`'s per-agent toolMix / skills / mcpServers correct for every agent (Codex, Gemini in this PR; others mechanical follow-up), not just Claude Code, so users see real data on their non-Claude work the first time the recap endpoint goes live.\n\n**Architecture:** The transcript parsers already normalize each agent's native format into a shared `TranscriptMessage[]` shape carrying `toolCalls?: ToolCall[]`. The current `extractToolMetrics` ignores that and re-scans raw JSONL with Claude-shaped assumptions (`type === \"assistant\"` + `mcp__*` prefix + `Skill` tool name), so non-Claude transcripts produce all-zero results. This plan inverts the dependency: each parser exposes an agent-specific tool classifier as optional methods on the existing `TranscriptParser` interface, and a refactored `extractToolMetricsFromSessions` consumes parser output instead of raw JSONL. A small backfill script re-extracts metrics for existing `repo_checkpoint_analyses` rows (no LLM calls — labels are already correct, only the deterministic post-processing was wrong).\n\n**Tech Stack:** TypeScript, Cloudflare Workers (workerd), Kysely + PlanetScale MySQL, Vitest, oxfmt, oxlint.\n\n---\n\n## Context: where this lands\n\n- **Repo:** `entirehq/entire.io` (the API + frontend monorepo)\n- **Branch:** new branch `fix/agent-aware-tool-metrics` off `main`\n- **Worktree:** `/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/entire.io/.worktrees/agent-tool-metrics` (create fresh)\n- **Pairs with:** PRs #1604 (recap endpoint) and #1737 (perf) — those should merge first; this PR fixes the producer side that feeds them.\n- **Rollout sequence:** merge #1604 → merge #1737 → merge this PR → run **tool-metrics backfill** (this PR's new script) → run **facet backfill** (already in #1737) → soak. The facet backfill must run **after** this one so it picks up the corrected `analysis_json`.\n- **Out of scope (deferred to follow-ups):**\n  - **Cursor classifier.** `cursor-parser.ts` only emits user/assistant text — it doesn't populate `TranscriptMessage.toolCalls`. A classifier on Cursor today is dead code. Surfacing tool calls in the Cursor parser is its own task; recap toolMix stays empty for Cursor users until that lands.\n  - **OpenCode / Droid / Copilot CLI / Kiro / Pi.** Their parsers already produce `toolCalls`, but user-impact priority is claude / codex / gemini. Adding classifiers later is a one-method-per-parser change.\n\n## What already exists in the codebase (we leverage, don't recreate)\n\n| Existing | Where | What we use it for |\n|---|---|---|\n| Real Codex transcript fixtures | `api/src/lib/transcript-parsers/codex-parser.test.ts` (431 lines, inline `rolloutTranscript` etc.) | Reuse for classifier tests — no separate JSON fixture file needed |\n| `extractToolMetrics` Claude-shaped tests | `api/src/lib/analysis-queue.test.ts:139-169` (4 cases) + `buildTranscript()` helper at `:127` | Adapt to new signature; delete `buildTranscript` (synthesizes the obsolete JSONL shape) |\n| Backfill script pattern | `api/scripts/backfill-search.ts` (576 lines, `--dry-run` / `--limit` / cursor pagination, MySQL bootstrap, no unit tests) | Mirror its shape directly. The repo convention is \"backfill scripts have no unit tests\" — we follow it for the production-bootstrap parts and add **one** focused test for the parts that ARE prone to subtle bugs (the JSON-merge semantics + SyntaxError narrowing) |\n| `TOOL_MIX_CATEGORY_KEYS` constant | `api/src/types.ts` | Add `ToolMixCategory` type alias + interface change here; no new file |\n| `loadCheckpointTranscript` | `api/src/lib/checkpoint-transcript.ts:323-348` | Single-arg-object signature — backfill script's `loadTranscript` closure mirrors `analysis-queue.ts:289-298` lookup pattern |\n\n## File structure\n\n| File | Purpose | Status |\n|---|---|---|\n| `api/src/types.ts` | Add `ToolMixCategory` type alias next to `TOOL_MIX_CATEGORY_KEYS` | modify |\n| `api/src/lib/transcript-parsers/types.ts` | Add three optional methods to `TranscriptParser`: `classifyTool`, `extractSkillFromTool`, `extractMcpServerFromTool` | modify |\n| `api/src/lib/transcript-parsers/claude-code-parser.ts` | Implement the three methods using Claude tool naming | modify |\n| `api/src/lib/transcript-parsers/codex-parser.ts` | Implement using Codex's tool naming (verified against real fixture) | modify |\n| `api/src/lib/transcript-parsers/gemini-parser.ts` | Implement using Gemini CLI's tool naming | modify |\n| `api/src/lib/analysis-queue.ts` | Replace `extractToolMetrics(sessionsMap)` with `extractToolMetricsFromSessions(sessions)`; update single in-tree caller | modify |\n| `api/src/lib/analysis-queue.test.ts` | Update existing extractToolMetrics tests to new signature; delete `buildTranscript` helper; add Codex coverage cases | modify |\n| `api/scripts/backfill-analysis-tool-metrics.ts` | New one-shot backfill script (no LLM calls) — mirrors `backfill-search.ts`'s flag/cursor/MySQL pattern | create |\n| `api/scripts/backfill-analysis-tool-metrics.test.ts` | One focused test: merge semantics preserve unrelated fields + SyntaxError narrowing | create |\n| `api/vitest.unit.config.ts` | Add the new test path | modify |\n\n**Files NOT in this plan (intentionally):** No `tool-categories.ts` (type lives in `types.ts`, no `defaultToolClassifier` needed because `?? \"other\"` handles it). No fallback-parser change (parser delegates to Claude already; classifier inherits via the optional-chaining fallback). No registry helper (existing `getParserForAgent` is sufficient). No separate Codex fixture JSON (existing inline fixture in `codex-parser.test.ts` is sufficient).\n\n---\n\n## Tasks\n\n## Chunk 1: Interface + Claude classifier (baseline preserved)\n\n### Task 1: Extend `TranscriptParser` with three optional methods + `ToolMixCategory` type\n\n**Files:**\n- Modify: `api/src/types.ts`\n- Modify: `api/src/lib/transcript-parsers/types.ts`\n\nThis is a type-system-only change. No runtime test — adding optional methods to an interface is exercised by the next task's actual implementation. The `ToolMixCategory` type alias lives next to `TOOL_MIX_CATEGORY_KEYS` since they're a unit.\n\n- [ ] **Step 1: Add the type alias to `api/src/types.ts`**\n\nFind the existing `TOOL_MIX_CATEGORY_KEYS` declaration (already exported). Right after it, add:\n\n```ts\nexport type ToolMixCategory = (typeof TOOL_MIX_CATEGORY_KEYS)[number]\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 2: Extend the parser interface**\n\nIn `api/src/lib/transcript-parsers/types.ts`, add the imports:\n\n```ts\nimport type { ToolCall, ToolMixCategory } from \"../../types\"\n```\n\nAfter the existing `parseFrom?` method on `TranscriptParser`, add:\n\n```ts\n  /**\n   * Classify a tool call into the shared toolMix bucket. Optional —\n   * undefined means \"I don't know how to classify this agent's tools\";\n   * callers default to \"other\" via the optional-chaining fallback.\n   */\n  classifyTool?(call: ToolCall): ToolMixCategory\n  /**\n   * Extract a skill name from a tool call, when applicable. Returns null\n   * when the call doesn't represent a skill invocation. Claude implements\n   * via the `Skill` tool; other agents return null until they grow the\n   * same surface.\n   */\n  extractSkillFromTool?(call: ToolCall): string | null\n  /**\n   * Extract an MCP server name from a tool call, when applicable. Returns\n   * null when the call isn't an MCP invocation. Claude parses the\n   * `mcp__server__tool` prefix convention; other agents return null\n   * until their parsers surface MCP server names.\n   */\n  extractMcpServerFromTool?(call: ToolCall): string | null\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 3: Typecheck to verify no other parsers broke**\n\nRun: `cd api && pnpm typecheck`\nExpected: clean. Optional methods on an interface don't force any change on existing implementations.\n\n- [ ] **Step 4: Commit**\n\n```bash\ngit add api/src/types.ts api/src/lib/transcript-parsers/types.ts\ngit commit -m \"feat(recap-tools): extend TranscriptParser with optional tool classifier surface\"\n```\n\n### Task 2: Implement Claude Code classifier (preserves baseline behavior)\n\n**Files:**\n- Modify: `api/src/lib/transcript-parsers/claude-code-parser.ts`\n- Modify: `api/src/lib/transcript-parsers/claude-code-parser.test.ts`\n\nThe Claude classifier reproduces exactly what `extractToolMetrics` does today (`Bash` → shell, `Read`/`Write`/`Edit` → fileOps, `Grep`/`Glob` → search, `Skill`/`Agent` → agent, `mcp__*` → mcp). After Task 5's refactor, this is the *only* code path that classifies Claude tools — keeping the mapping byte-for-byte ensures Claude users see no change.\n\n- [ ] **Step 1: Write failing tests**\n\nAdd to `claude-code-parser.test.ts`:\n\n```ts\nimport type { ToolCall } from \"../../types\"\n\ndescribe(\"ClaudeCodeParser tool classification\", () => {\n  const parser = new ClaudeCodeParser()\n  const make = (name: string, input: Record<string, unknown> = {}) =>\n    ({ id: \"x\", name, input, timestamp: \"\" }) as ToolCall\n\n  it(\"classifies Bash as shell\", () => {\n    expect(parser.classifyTool!(make(\"Bash\"))).toBe(\"shell\")\n  })\n  it.each([\"Read\", \"Write\", \"Edit\"])(\"classifies %s as fileOps\", (name) => {\n    expect(parser.classifyTool!(make(name))).toBe(\"fileOps\")\n  })\n  it.each([\"Grep\", \"Glob\"])(\"classifies %s as search\", (name) => {\n    expect(parser.classifyTool!(make(name))).toBe(\"search\")\n  })\n  it.each([\"Skill\", \"Agent\"])(\"classifies %s as agent\", (name) => {\n    expect(parser.classifyTool!(make(name))).toBe(\"agent\")\n  })\n  it(\"classifies mcp__*** as mcp\", () => {\n    expect(parser.classifyTool!(make(\"mcp__github__list_issues\"))).toBe(\"mcp\")\n  })\n  it(\"classifies unknown tools as other\", () => {\n    expect(parser.classifyTool!(make(\"WebFetch\"))).toBe(\"other\")\n  })\n\n  it(\"extracts skill from Skill tool input\", () => {\n    expect(parser.extractSkillFromTool!(make(\"Skill\", { skill: \"debugging\" }))).toBe(\n      \"debugging\",\n    )\n    expect(parser.extractSkillFromTool!(make(\"Bash\"))).toBeNull()\n    expect(parser.extractSkillFromTool!(make(\"Skill\", {}))).toBeNull()\n  })\n\n  it(\"extracts mcp server from mcp__server__tool\", () => {\n    expect(parser.extractMcpServerFromTool!(make(\"mcp__github__list_issues\"))).toBe(\"github\")\n    expect(parser.extractMcpServerFromTool!(make(\"Bash\"))).toBeNull()\n  })\n})\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 2: Run tests to verify they fail**\n\nRun: `cd api && pnpm vitest run src/lib/transcript-parsers/claude-code-parser.test.ts`\nExpected: FAIL — methods not implemented.\n\n- [ ] **Step 3: Implement on the `ClaudeCodeParser` class**\n\nAdd the import and three methods:\n\n```ts\nimport type { ToolMixCategory } from \"../../types\"\n// (ToolCall is already imported)\n\n// inside the class:\nclassifyTool(call: ToolCall): ToolMixCategory {\n  const name = call.name\n  if (name === \"Bash\") return \"shell\"\n  if (name === \"Read\" || name === \"Write\" || name === \"Edit\") return \"fileOps\"\n  if (name === \"Grep\" || name === \"Glob\") return \"search\"\n  if (name === \"Skill\" || name === \"Agent\") return \"agent\"\n  if (name.startsWith(\"mcp__\")) return \"mcp\"\n  return \"other\"\n}\n\nextractSkillFromTool(call: ToolCall): string | null {\n  if (call.name !== \"Skill\") return null\n  const skill = (call.input as Record<string, unknown>)?.skill\n  return typeof skill === \"string\" && skill.length > 0 ? skill : null\n}\n\nextractMcpServerFromTool(call: ToolCall): string | null {\n  if (!call.name.startsWith(\"mcp__\")) return null\n  const segments = call.name.split(\"__\")\n  return segments.length >= 3 && segments[1] ? segments[1] : null\n}\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 4: Run tests to verify they pass**\n\nRun: `cd api && pnpm vitest run src/lib/transcript-parsers/claude-code-parser.test.ts`\nExpected: PASS.\n\n- [ ] **Step 5: Commit**\n\n```bash\ngit add api/src/lib/transcript-parsers/claude-code-parser.ts api/src/lib/transcript-parsers/claude-code-parser.test.ts\ngit commit -m \"feat(recap-tools): ClaudeCodeParser exposes tool classifier (baseline)\"\n```\n\n## Chunk 2: Codex + Gemini classifiers\n\n### Task 3: Implement Codex classifier (using existing inline fixtures)\n\n**Files:**\n- Modify: `api/src/lib/transcript-parsers/codex-parser.ts`\n- Modify: `api/src/lib/transcript-parsers/codex-parser.test.ts`\n\n`codex-parser.test.ts` already has a real `rolloutTranscript` constant with `apply_patch`, `custom_tool_call`, `function_call` payloads. Task 5's classifier tests build on top of that fixture rather than capturing a separate JSON file. Codex tool-name vocabulary, derived from real production transcripts (the cli repo's checkpoint `7a9387cf9003`):\n\n| Codex tool name | Bucket | Reasoning |\n|---|---|---|\n| `exec_command`, `local_shell_call`, `write_stdin`, `bash`, `shell` | shell | Codex's primary shell paths (`local_shell_call` is the parser's synthesized name for `local_shell_call` payloads) |\n| `apply_patch`, `read_file`, `write_file`, `edit` | fileOps | Patch/file tools |\n| `update_plan` | agent | Plan/track-list management |\n| Names starting with `_` | mcp | Codex MCP-tool naming convention (`_list_pull_request_review_threads`, `_fetch_pr_comments`) |\n| anything else | other | Explicit unknown |\n\n- [ ] **Step 1: Write failing tests**\n\nAdd to `codex-parser.test.ts`:\n\n```ts\nimport type { ToolCall } from \"../../types\"\n\ndescribe(\"CodexParser tool classification\", () => {\n  const parser = new CodexParser()\n  const make = (name: string) => ({ id: \"x\", name, input: {}, timestamp: \"\" }) as ToolCall\n\n  it(\"classifies exec_command (Codex's primary shell tool) as shell\", () => {\n    expect(parser.classifyTool!(make(\"exec_command\"))).toBe(\"shell\")\n  })\n  it.each([\"local_shell_call\", \"write_stdin\", \"bash\", \"shell\"])(\n    \"classifies %s as shell\",\n    (name) => {\n      expect(parser.classifyTool!(make(name))).toBe(\"shell\")\n    },\n  )\n  it.each([\"apply_patch\", \"read_file\", \"write_file\", \"edit\"])(\n    \"classifies %s as fileOps\",\n    (name) => {\n      expect(parser.classifyTool!(make(name))).toBe(\"fileOps\")\n    },\n  )\n  it(\"classifies update_plan as agent\", () => {\n    expect(parser.classifyTool!(make(\"update_plan\"))).toBe(\"agent\")\n  })\n  it(\"classifies underscore-prefixed names as mcp (Codex MCP convention)\", () => {\n    expect(parser.classifyTool!(make(\"_list_pull_request_review_threads\"))).toBe(\"mcp\")\n    expect(parser.classifyTool!(make(\"_fetch_pr_comments\"))).toBe(\"mcp\")\n  })\n  it(\"returns 'other' for unrecognized tools\", () => {\n    expect(parser.classifyTool!(make(\"definitely_not_a_codex_tool\"))).toBe(\"other\")\n  })\n  it(\"returns null for skill / mcp-server extraction (Codex parser doesn't surface them today)\", () => {\n    expect(parser.extractSkillFromTool!(make(\"exec_command\"))).toBeNull()\n    expect(parser.extractMcpServerFromTool!(make(\"exec_command\"))).toBeNull()\n  })\n\n  // Integration with the existing rolloutTranscript fixture: every tool call\n  // the existing parser produces must classify into a non-`other` bucket.\n  // This catches the \"everything is `other`\" failure mode against real data.\n  it(\"classifies every tool call from the existing rolloutTranscript fixture into a non-other bucket\", () => {\n    const { messages } = parser.parse(rolloutTranscript)\n    const toolCalls = messages.flatMap((m) => m.toolCalls ?? [])\n    expect(toolCalls.length).toBeGreaterThan(0)\n    const dropped = toolCalls.filter((c) => parser.classifyTool!(c) === \"other\")\n    expect(dropped.map((c) => c.name)).toEqual([])\n  })\n})\n```\n\nThe last assertion uses the existing `rolloutTranscript` constant (already in this test file). If the parser produces tool calls whose names aren't in the classifier's mapping, the test fails with the offending names — actionable.\n\n- [ ] **Step 2: Run tests to verify they fail**\n\nRun: `cd api && pnpm vitest run src/lib/transcript-parsers/codex-parser.test.ts`\nExpected: FAIL — methods not implemented.\n\n- [ ] **Step 3: Implement on `CodexParser` class**\n\n```ts\nimport type { ToolMixCategory } from \"../../types\"\n// (ToolCall already imported)\n\n// inside the class:\nclassifyTool(call: ToolCall): ToolMixCategory {\n  const name = call.name\n  if (\n    name === \"exec_command\" ||\n    name === \"local_shell_call\" ||\n    name === \"write_stdin\" ||\n    name === \"bash\" ||\n    name === \"shell\"\n  ) {\n    return \"shell\"\n  }\n  if (\n    name === \"apply_patch\" ||\n    name === \"read_file\" ||\n    name === \"write_file\" ||\n    name === \"edit\"\n  ) {\n    return \"fileOps\"\n  }\n  if (name === \"update_plan\") return \"agent\"\n  if (name.startsWith(\"_\")) return \"mcp\" // Codex MCP-tool naming convention\n  return \"other\"\n}\n\nextractSkillFromTool(_call: ToolCall): string | null {\n  return null // Codex has no Skill-tool equivalent\n}\n\nextractMcpServerFromTool(_call: ToolCall): string | null {\n  // Codex transcripts contain `mcp_tool_call_end` payloads but the parser\n  // doesn't currently surface a server name in toolCalls[]. Returning null\n  // is correct today; surfacing names is a follow-up parser change.\n  return null\n}\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 4: Run tests to verify they pass**\n\nRun: `cd api && pnpm vitest run src/lib/transcript-parsers/codex-parser.test.ts`\nExpected: PASS, including the rolloutTranscript-coverage assertion.\n\n- [ ] **Step 5: Commit**\n\n```bash\ngit add api/src/lib/transcript-parsers/codex-parser.ts api/src/lib/transcript-parsers/codex-parser.test.ts\ngit commit -m \"feat(recap-tools): CodexParser exposes tool classifier\"\n```\n\n### Task 4: Implement Gemini classifier\n\n**Files:**\n- Modify: `api/src/lib/transcript-parsers/gemini-parser.ts`\n- Create: `api/src/lib/transcript-parsers/gemini-parser.test.ts` (if not present)\n\nGemini CLI tool names from the documented spec: `run_shell_command`, `read_file`, `write_file`, `replace`, `glob`, `search_file_content`, `list_directory`, `web_fetch`, `save_memory`. We don't have a Gemini fixture in-tree, so the test relies on the documented vocabulary.\n\n- [ ] **Step 1: Write failing tests**\n\n```ts\nimport { describe, expect, it } from \"vitest\"\nimport type { ToolCall } from \"../../types\"\nimport { GeminiParser } from \"./gemini-parser\"\n\ndescribe(\"GeminiParser tool classification\", () => {\n  const parser = new GeminiParser()\n  const make = (name: string) => ({ id: \"x\", name, input: {}, timestamp: \"\" }) as ToolCall\n\n  it(\"classifies run_shell_command as shell\", () => {\n    expect(parser.classifyTool!(make(\"run_shell_command\"))).toBe(\"shell\")\n  })\n  it.each([\"read_file\", \"write_file\", \"replace\"])(\"classifies %s as fileOps\", (name) => {\n    expect(parser.classifyTool!(make(name))).toBe(\"fileOps\")\n  })\n  it.each([\"glob\", \"search_file_content\", \"list_directory\"])(\n    \"classifies %s as search\",\n    (name) => {\n      expect(parser.classifyTool!(make(name))).toBe(\"search\")\n    },\n  )\n  it(\"returns 'other' for unrecognized tools\", () => {\n    expect(parser.classifyTool!(make(\"totally_made_up_tool\"))).toBe(\"other\")\n  })\n})\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 2: Run tests to verify they fail**\n\nRun: `cd api && pnpm vitest run src/lib/transcript-parsers/gemini-parser.test.ts`\nExpected: FAIL.\n\n- [ ] **Step 3: Implement on `GeminiParser`**\n\n```ts\nimport type { ToolMixCategory } from \"../../types\"\n\n// inside the class:\nclassifyTool(call: ToolCall): ToolMixCategory {\n  const name = call.name\n  if (name === \"run_shell_command\") return \"shell\"\n  if (name === \"read_file\" || name === \"write_file\" || name === \"replace\") return \"fileOps\"\n  if (name === \"glob\" || name === \"search_file_content\" || name === \"list_directory\") {\n    return \"search\"\n  }\n  return \"other\"\n}\n\nextractSkillFromTool(_call: ToolCall): string | null {\n  return null\n}\n\nextractMcpServerFromTool(_call: ToolCall): string | null {\n  return null\n}\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 4: Run tests to verify they pass**\n\nRun: `cd api && pnpm vitest run src/lib/transcript-parsers/gemini-parser.test.ts`\nExpected: PASS.\n\n- [ ] **Step 5: Commit**\n\n```bash\ngit add api/src/lib/transcript-parsers/gemini-parser.ts api/src/lib/transcript-parsers/gemini-parser.test.ts\ngit commit -m \"feat(recap-tools): GeminiParser exposes tool classifier\"\n```\n\n## Chunk 3: Refactor `extractToolMetrics`\n\n### Task 5: Replace `extractToolMetrics` with `extractToolMetricsFromSessions`\n\n**Files:**\n- Modify: `api/src/lib/analysis-queue.ts`\n- Modify: `api/src/lib/analysis-queue.test.ts`\n\nThe current `extractToolMetrics(sessionsMap)` re-parses raw JSONL inside the function with hardcoded Claude rules. It's called once, from `decorateReviewWithMetrics` at `analysis-queue.ts:159`. We replace it with `extractToolMetricsFromSessions(sessions)` taking parsed `SessionTranscript[]` (already available as `loaded.sessions` on the same line). Verified during planning:\n\n- `LoadedCheckpointTranscript.sessions: SessionTranscript[]` at `api/src/lib/checkpoint-transcript.ts:308`\n- `SessionTranscript { sessionId, agent, messages: TranscriptMessage[], ... }` at `api/src/types.ts:437-455`\n- Every parser that produces tool calls (Claude/Codex/Gemini/OpenCode/Droid/Copilot) populates `TranscriptMessage.toolCalls` — Cursor doesn't (out of scope, see context)\n\nExisting tests at `analysis-queue.test.ts:139-169` test the OLD signature. They use a `buildTranscript()` helper at `:127` that synthesizes Claude JSONL. After the refactor, both the helper and the old-shape tests are obsolete — the new tests run real parsers against real inputs.\n\n- [ ] **Step 1: Write failing tests covering Claude + Codex paths through the new function**\n\nReplace the existing `describe(\"extractToolMetrics\", ...)` block in `analysis-queue.test.ts` (lines 139-169) and the `buildTranscript()` helper (lines 127-137) with:\n\n```ts\nimport { ClaudeCodeParser } from \"./transcript-parsers/claude-code-parser\"\nimport { CodexParser } from \"./transcript-parsers/codex-parser\"\nimport { extractToolMetricsFromSessions } from \"./analysis-queue\"\n\ndescribe(\"extractToolMetricsFromSessions — agent-aware\", () => {\n  it(\"returns null toolProfile when sessions have no tool calls\", () => {\n    expect(\n      extractToolMetricsFromSessions([{ agent: \"Claude Code\", messages: [] }]).toolProfile,\n    ).toBeNull()\n  })\n\n  it(\"classifies Claude tool calls under Claude rules\", () => {\n    const claudeJsonl = [\n      JSON.stringify({\n        type: \"assistant\",\n        message: {\n          content: [\n            { type: \"tool_use\", id: \"1\", name: \"Bash\", input: { command: \"ls\" } },\n            { type: \"tool_use\", id: \"2\", name: \"Read\", input: { file: \"x.ts\" } },\n            { type: \"tool_use\", id: \"3\", name: \"mcp__github__list_issues\", input: {} },\n            { type: \"tool_use\", id: \"4\", name: \"Skill\", input: { skill: \"debugging\" } },\n          ],\n        },\n        timestamp: \"2026-04-30T00:00:00Z\",\n      }),\n    ].join(\"\\n\")\n    const messages = new ClaudeCodeParser().parse(claudeJsonl).messages\n    const m = extractToolMetricsFromSessions([{ agent: \"Claude Code\", messages }])\n\n    expect(m.toolProfile?.categories.shell.count).toBe(1)\n    expect(m.toolProfile?.categories.fileOps.count).toBe(1)\n    expect(m.toolProfile?.categories.mcp.count).toBe(1)\n    expect(m.toolProfile?.categories.agent.count).toBe(1)\n    expect(m.skillsUsed).toEqual([\"debugging\"])\n    expect(m.mcpServersUsed).toEqual([{ name: \"github\", count: 1 }])\n  })\n\n  it(\"classifies Codex tool calls under Codex rules (regression test for the all-zeros bug)\", () => {\n    const codexJsonl = [\n      JSON.stringify({\n        timestamp: \"2026-04-30T00:00:00Z\",\n        type: \"response_item\",\n        payload: {\n          type: \"function_call\",\n          name: \"exec_command\",\n          call_id: \"c1\",\n          arguments: JSON.stringify({ command: \"ls\" }),\n        },\n      }),\n      JSON.stringify({\n        timestamp: \"2026-04-30T00:00:01Z\",\n        type: \"response_item\",\n        payload: {\n          type: \"function_call\",\n          name: \"apply_patch\",\n          call_id: \"c2\",\n          arguments: JSON.stringify({}),\n        },\n      }),\n      JSON.stringify({\n        timestamp: \"2026-04-30T00:00:02Z\",\n        type: \"response_item\",\n        payload: {\n          type: \"function_call\",\n          name: \"_list_pull_request_review_threads\",\n          call_id: \"c3\",\n          arguments: JSON.stringify({}),\n        },\n      }),\n    ].join(\"\\n\")\n    const messages = new CodexParser().parse(codexJsonl).messages\n    const m = extractToolMetricsFromSessions([{ agent: \"Codex\", messages }])\n\n    // Real Codex tool names produce real bucket counts. Pre-refactor this\n    // returned all zeros because extractToolMetrics filtered on Claude's\n    // `type === \"assistant\"` shape that Codex never emits.\n    expect(m.toolProfile?.categories.shell.count).toBe(1) // exec_command\n    expect(m.toolProfile?.categories.fileOps.count).toBe(1) // apply_patch\n    expect(m.toolProfile?.catego