three optional methods: `classifyTool`, `extractSkillFromTool`, `extractMcpServerFromTool`\n- Implementations on Claude / Codex / Gemini parsers, with Codex coverage pinned to the existing inline rolloutTranscript fixture (no zeros for production data)\n- `extractToolMetricsFromSessions` replaces `extractToolMetrics` — consumes parsed `TranscriptMessage[]` instead of raw JSONL, dispatches via each session's agent. No backwards-compat bridge; the single in-tree caller is updated in the same commit. The obsolete `buildTranscript` test helper is deleted.\n- New backfill script `scripts/backfill-analysis-tool-metrics.ts` re-runs the extractor against existing transcripts and overwrites only `toolProfile`, `skillsUsed`, `mcpServersUsed` in `analysis_json`. Cursor-paginated, idempotent, supports `--dry-run` and `--limit=N`. NO LLM calls — labels are already correct.\n\n## Pairs with\n\n- #1604 (recap endpoint)\n- #1737 (perf via SQL aggregation)\n\nLand order: #1604 → #1737 → this PR → run **tool-metrics backfill** (this PR) → run **facet backfill** (from #1737) → soak. Facet backfill must run AFTER this one so it picks up the corrected analysis_json.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] Per-parser unit tests for `classifyTool` / `extractSkillFromTool` / `extractMcpServerFromTool`\n- [x] Codex classifier coverage assertion: every tool call in the existing rolloutTranscript fixture lands in a non-`other` bucket\n- [x] `extractToolMetricsFromSessions` integration: pinned bucket counts for representative Claude and Codex inputs (`.toBe(1)`, not `> 0`)\n- [x] Backfill script: merge semantics preserve labels + scalars, narrow `SyntaxError` catch with infra-error propagation\n- [x] CI gauntlet: format → openapi/sdk drift → DB drift → lint (API + frontend) → typecheck → test:run --coverage\nEOF\n)\"\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 9: Verify CI**\n\nAfter ~3-5 min:\n\n```bash\ngh pr checks <PR#> --repo entirehq/entire.io\n```\n\nExpected: all green. If any drift check fails, the local gauntlet missed it — note for the next PR.\n\n---\n\n## Notes for execution\n\n- **Use a fresh worktree:** `git worktree add /Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/entire.io/.worktrees/agent-tool-metrics -b fix/agent-aware-tool-metrics origin/main` before starting.\n- **Follow TDD strictly:** every implementation task starts with a failing test. If the test in step 1 doesn't fail at step 2, the test is wrong (or the code already does the thing) — fix before proceeding.\n- **Each task ends in one commit.** No batched commits.\n- **No backwards-compatibility shims.** The single in-tree caller of the old `extractToolMetrics` is updated in the same commit that introduces `extractToolMetricsFromSessions`. The deprecated `buildTranscript` test helper is deleted.\n- **Never re-run the LLM in backfill.** That would burn Anthropic budget. The script only re-extracts the deterministic post-processing (`extractToolMetricsFromSessions`) and overwrites three specific fields in `analysis_json`.\n- **The Codex `rolloutTranscript` fixture in `codex-parser.test.ts` is the load-bearing test signal** for non-Claude correctness. If the classifier doesn't categorize every observed name into a non-empty bucket, that's a real coverage hole worth fixing before commit.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8178,"cache_read_input_tokens":856219,"output_tokens":23148,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":8178,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":23148,"cache_read_input_tokens":856219,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8178,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":8178},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Caa1cZfQM6A5FxprGCPRY","type":"assistant","uui