il their parsers surface MCP server names.\n92\t   */\n93\t  extractMcpServerFromTool?(call: ToolCall): string | null\n94\t```\n95\t\n96\t- [ ] **Step 2: Typecheck to verify no other parsers broke**\n97\t\n98\tRun: `cd api && pnpm typecheck`\n99\tExpected: clean. Optional methods on an interface don't force any change on existing implementations.\n100\t\n101\t- [ ] **Step 3: Commit**\n102\t\n103\t```bash\n104\tgit add api/src/lib/transcript-parsers/types.ts\n105\tgit commit -m \"feat(recap-tools): extend TranscriptParser with optional tool classifier surface\"\n106\t```\n107\t\n108\t### Task 2: Implement Claude Code classifier (preserves baseline behavior)\n109\t\n110\t**Files:**\n111\t- Modify: `api/src/lib/transcript-parsers/claude-code-parser.ts`\n112\t- Modify: `api/src/lib/transcript-parsers/claude-code-parser.test.ts`\n113\t\n114\tThe Claude classifier reproduces exactly what `extractToolMetrics` does today (`Bash` → shell, `Read`/`Write`/`Edit` → fileOps, `Grep`/`Glob` → search, `Skill`/`Agent` → agent, `mcp__*` → mcp). After Task 5's refactor, this is the *only* code path that classifies Claude tools — keeping the mapping byte-for-byte ensures Claude users see no change.\n115\t\n116\t- [ ] **Step 1: Write failing tests**\n117\t\n118\tAdd to `claude-code-parser.test.ts`:\n119\t\n120\t```ts\n121\timport type { ToolCall } from \"../../types\"\n122\t\n123\tdescribe(\"ClaudeCodeParser tool classification\", () => {\n124\t  const parser = new ClaudeCodeParser()\n125\t  const make = (name: string, input: Record<string, unknown> = {}) =>\n126\t    ({ id: \"x\", name, input, timestamp: \"\" }) as ToolCall\n127\t\n128\t  it(\"classifies Bash as shell\", () => {\n129\t    expect(parser.classifyTool!(make(\"Bash\"))).toBe(\"shell\")\n130\t  })\n131\t  it.each([\"Read\", \"Write\", \"Edit\"])(\"classifies %s as fileOps\", (name) => {\n132\t    expect(parser.classifyTool!(make(name))).toBe(\"fileOps\")\n133\t  })\n134\t  it.each([\"Grep\", \"Glob\"])(\"classifies %s as search\", (name) => {\n135\t    expect(parser.classifyTool!(make(name))).toBe(\"search\")\n136\t  })\n137\t  it.each([\"Skill\", \"Agent\"])(\"classifies %s as agent\", (name) => {\n138\t    expect(parser.classifyTool!(make(name))).toBe(\"agent\")\n139\t  })\n140\t  it(\"classifies mcp__*** as mcp\", () => {\n141\t    expect(parser.classifyTool!(make(\"mcp__github__list_issues\"))).toBe(\"mcp\")\n142\t  })\n143\t  it(\"classifies unknown tools as other\", () => {\n144\t    expect(parser.classifyTool!(make(\"WebFetch\"))).toBe(\"other\")\n145\t  })\n146\t\n147\t  it(\"extracts skill from Skill tool input\", () => {\n148\t    expect(parser.extractSkillFromTool!(make(\"Skill\", { skill: \"debugging\" }))).toBe(\n149\t      \"debugging\",\n150\t    )\n151\t    expect(parser.extractSkillFromTool!(make(\"Bash\"))).toBeNull()\n152\t    expect(parser.extractSkillFromTool!(make(\"Skill\", {}))).toBeNull()\n153\t  })\n154\t\n155\t  it(\"extracts mcp server from mcp__server__tool\", () => {\n156\t    expect(parser.extractMcpServerFromTool!(make(\"mcp__github__list_issues\"))).toBe(\"github\")\n157\t    expect(parser.extractMcpServerFromTool!(make(\"Bash\"))).toBeNull()\n158\t  })\n159\t})\n160\t```\n161\t"}]},"uuid":"1fd02e2e-ac11-433a-848b-ec2f7322a57a","timestamp":"2026-04-30T13:53:18.468Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/entire-activity/docs/superpowers/plans/2026-04-30-agent-aware-tool-metrics.md","content":"## Tasks\n\n## Chunk 1: Interface + Claude classifier (baseline preserved)\n\n### Task 1: Extend `TranscriptParser` with three optional methods\n\n**Files:**\n- Modify: `api/src/lib/transcript-parsers/types.ts`\n\nThis is a type-system-only change. No runtime test — adding optional methods to an interface is exercised by the next task's actual implementation. The shared `ToolMixCategoryKey` type alias **already exists** at `api/src/types.ts:676` — we reuse it, no new type to add.\n\n- [ ] **Step 1: Extend the parser interface**\n\nIn `api/src/lib/transcript-parsers/types.ts`, add the imports:\n\n```ts\nimport type { ToolCall, ToolMixCategoryKey } from \"../../types\"\n```\n\nAfter the existing `parseFrom?` method on `TranscriptParser`, add:\n\n```ts\n  /**\n   * Classify a tool call into the shared toolMix bucket. Optional —\n   * undefined means \"I don't know how to classify this agent's tools\";\n   * callers default to \"other\" via the optional-chaining fallback.\n   */\n  classifyTool?(call: ToolCall): ToolMixCategoryKey\n  /**\n   * Extract a skill name from a tool call, when applicable. Returns null\n   * when the call doesn't represent a skill invocation. Claude implements\n   * via the `Skill` tool; other agents return null until they grow the\n   * same surface.\n   */\n  extractSkillFromTool?(call: ToolCall): string | null\n  /**\n   * Extract an MCP server name from a tool call, when applicable. Returns\n   * null when the call isn't an MCP invocation. Claude parses the\n   * `mcp__server__tool` prefix convention; other agents return null\n   * until their parsers surface MCP server names.\n   */\n  extractMcpServerFromTool?(call: ToolCall): string | null\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 2: Typecheck to verify no other parsers broke**\n\nRun: `cd api && pnpm typecheck`\nExpected: clean. Optional methods on an interface don't force any change on existing implementations.\n\n- [ ] **Step 3: Commit**\n\n```bash\ngit add api/src/lib/transcript-parsers/types.ts\ngit commit -m \"feat(recap-tools): extend TranscriptParser with optional tool classifier surface\"\n```\n\n### Task 2: Implement Claude Code classifier (preserves baseline behavior)\n\n**Files:**\n- Modify: `api/src/lib/transcript-parsers/claude-code-parser.ts`\n- Modify: `api/src/lib/transcript-parsers/claude-code-parser.test.ts`\n\nThe Claude classifier reproduces exactly what `extractToolMetrics` does today (`Bash` → shell, `Read`/`Write`/`Edit` → fileOps, `Grep`/`Glob` → search, `Skill`/`Agent` → agent, `mcp__*` → mcp). After Task 5's refactor, this is the *only* code path that classifies Claude tools — keeping the mapping byte-for-byte ensures Claude users see no change.\n\n- [ ] **Step 1: Write failing tests**\n\nAdd to `claude-code-parser.test.ts`:\n\n```ts\nimport type { ToolCall } from \"../../types\"\n\ndescribe(\"ClaudeCodeParser tool classification\", () => {\n  const parser = new ClaudeCodeParser()\n  const make = (name: string, input: Record<string, unknown> = {}) =>\n    ({ id: \"x\", name, input, timestamp: \"\" }) as ToolCall\n\n  it(\"classifies Bash as shell\", () => {\n    expect(parser.classifyTool!(make(\"Bash\"))).toBe(\"shell\")\n  })\n  it.each([\"Read\", \"Write\", \"Edit\"])(\"classifies %s as fileOps\", (name) => {\n    expect(parser.classifyTool!(make(name))).toBe(\"fileOps\")\n  })\n  it.each([\"Grep\", \"Glob\"])(\"classifies %s as search\", (name) => {\n    expect(parser.classifyTool!(make(name))).toBe(\"search\")\n  })\n  it.each([\"Skill\", \"Agent\"])(\"classifies %s as agent\", (name) => {\n    expect(parser.classifyTool!(make(name))).toBe(\"agent\")\n  })\n  it(\"classifies mcp__*** as mcp\", () => {\n    expect(parser.classifyTool!(make(\"mcp__github__list_issues\"))).toBe(\"mcp\")\n  })\n  it(\"classifies unknown tools as other\", () => {\n    expect(parser.classifyTool!(make(\"WebFetch\"))).toBe(\"other\")\n  })\n\n  it(\"extracts skill from Skill tool input\", () => {\n    expect(parser.extractSkillFromTool!(make(\"Skill\", { skill: \"debugging\" }))).toBe(\n      \"debugging\",\n    )\n    expect(parser.extractSkillFromTool!(make(\"Bash\"))).toBeNull()\n    expect(parser.extractSkillFromTool!(make(\"Skill\", {}))).toBeNull()\n  })\n\n  it(\"extracts mcp server from mcp__server__tool\", () => {\n    expect(parser.extractMcpServerFromTool!(make(\"mcp__github__list_issues\"))).toBe(\"github\")\n    expect(parser.extractMcpServerFromTool!(make(\"Bash\"))).toBeNull()\n  })\n})\n```\n","numLines":110,"startLine":52,"t