const dryRun = process.argv.includes(\"--dry-run\")\n\n  const result = await runBackfill({ db: kysely, loadTranscript }, { max, dryRun })\n  console.log(`done. ${JSON.stringify(result)}`)\n  await kysely.destroy()\n}\n\nif (process.argv[1] && /backfill-analysis-tool-metrics\\.ts$/.test(process.argv[1])) {\n  main().catch((err) => {\n    console.error(err)\n    process.exit(1)\n  })\n}\n```\n\nNOTE on the `main()` function:\n- The exact API of `createCheckpointsNamespace` / `createReposNamespace` / `db.checkpoints.findById` / `db.repos.getById` / `getCheckpointRepoName` / `loadCheckpointTranscript` may differ slightly from the plan. **Read `api/src/lib/checkpoint-transcript.ts` and `analysis-queue.ts`'s production lookup pattern (around lines 289-298) before writing `main()`** — mirror what's actually there. The shape of `location.commit` and the return shape may differ. If the actual shape is different, fix the call sites in `main()` to match. The exported `runBackfill` and `BackfillDeps` types are what the test imports — those need to stay stable.\n\n### Step 4: Add the test path to the curated unit suite\n\nRead `api/vitest.unit.config.ts` first. It has an `include` array of test paths. Add `\"scripts/backfill-analysis-tool-metrics.test.ts\"` to that array (alphabetized if the existing entries are sorted; otherwise append).\n\n### Step 5: Run tests to verify they pass\n\n`cd api && pnpm vitest run scripts/backfill-analysis-tool-metrics.test.ts`\n\nExpected: PASS — both tests green.\n\nIf they fail, debug:\n- Mock chain mismatch → adjust the mock to match the actual Kysely call sequence\n- Type errors on `BackfillDeps` cast → fix the `as BackfillDeps` cast or the function signature\n- Import errors → verify all paths\n\n### Step 6: Format\n\n```bash\ncd /Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/entire.io/.worktrees/agent-tool-metrics\npnpm format api/scripts/backfill-analysis-tool-metrics.ts api/scripts/backfill-analysis-tool-metrics.test.ts\n```\n\nIf 