 through.\n10\t\n11\t**How to apply:**\n12\t- New agent integration → Classifier with `Provider` only, no `Phrases`, until a research pass captures real stderr.\n13\t- Reviewing existing Classifiers → if phrases were added without a fixture-based test asserting the exact substring is produced by the real CLI, propose removing them.\n14\t- User message `<prefix>: <stderr>` with prefix=\"failed to generate the summary\" is acceptable; the CLI's stderr carries the remediation.\n15\t- Gemini and Codex phrases are verbatim from a 2026-04-20 research pass and are OK to keep.\n16\t- Claude is the exception — its structured envelope yields terse `Message` values without remediation, so `providersNeedingSynthesizedRemediation[ClaudeCode] = true` still applies.\n17\t"}]},"uuid":"fea5d87d-735e-41db-ba1e-e01871464a33","timestamp":"2026-04-30T16:21:09.731Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/peytonmontei/.claude/projects/-Users-peytonmontei-Documents-entire-devenv-entireio-cli/memory/feedback_error_classification_phrases.md","content":"---\nname: No speculative phrases in text-gen error Classifiers\ndescription: For agent text-generation error classification in cmd/entire/cli/agent/*, don't seed per-agent phrases without verbatim stderr fixtures; rely on HTTP-status baseline + verbatim stderr passthrough.\ntype: feedback\noriginSessionId: 10542774-5ed9-46bc-bc15-29deec90c88e\n---\nWhen adding or updating a per-agent `Classifier` in `cmd/entire/cli/agent/<agent>/error.go`, do NOT invent speculative `PhraseRule` entries (e.g. \"rate limit\", \"quota\", \"not authenticated\") without a captured-stderr fixture proving that CLI actually emits that exact substring. Ship the Classifier with zero `Phrases` if no fixtures exist.\n\n**Why:** Peyton explicitly flagged this on 2026-04-21 during the Chunk 5/6 cursor+copilot migrations on branch `feat/all-agents-summary-error-handling`. The CLI's own stderr is already captured verbatim into `TextGenError.Message` and shown to the user via `renderTextGenError` — so classification only affects the short prefix label (\"authentication failed\" vs \"failed to generate the summary\"), not the remediation text the user actually acts on. Guessing at phrases risks miscategorizing stderr that happens to contain those words in non-matching contexts, which is strictly worse than the Unknown fallthrough. The shared HTTP-status baseline (401/403/429/400/404) in `text_gen_error.go` already covers the load-bearing cases for any CLI that passes upstream HTTP status through.\n\n**How to apply:**\n- New agent integration → Classifier with `Provider` only, no `Phrases`, until a research pass captures real stderr.\n- Reviewing existing Classifiers → if phrases were added without a fixture-based test asserting the exact substring is produced by the real CLI, propose removing them.\n- User message `<prefix>: <stderr>` with prefix=\"failed to generate the summary\" is acceptable; the CLI's stderr carries the remediation.\n- Gemini and Codex phrases are verbatim from a 2026-04-20 research pass and are OK to keep.\n- Claude is the exception — its structured envelope yields terse `Message` values without remediation, so `providersNeedingSynthesizedRemediation[ClaudeCode] = true` still applies.\n","numLines":17,"startLine":1,"totalLines":17}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"2e7a3cf1-0418-4bec-9893-a0dbdcbfac27","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/entire-activity","sessionId":"a654b6ca-4957-4d7c-8c99-62db313ff0a0","version":"2.1.119","gitBranch":"entire-activity","slug":"vectorized-whistling-bonbon"}
